{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c5e9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3cf-5753-7b41-a2b3-ce03595a21fa"},"sequence":335,"recorded_at":1780531400000665,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3d0-95c5-7e12-867a-d743b5e3260b"},"task_id":"01a0b3d0-95c5-7e12-867a-d743b5e3260b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3d0-95c5-7e12-867a-d743b5e3260b","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev1/results.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-32ypr2 Results — test-unknown-encrypted-and-incomplete-events\n2|\n3|Status: ready for review. Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree\n4|(`task-board/story/STORY-260830-1cyj0q`); no commit on the Story branch.\n5|Branch tip after refresh: `3005d78` (replayed `TASK-260830-2g5be6`\n6|checkpoint over trunk `c3aae73`); `origin/main` is `c3aae73` at handoff.\n7|\n8|## Start-of-run recovery (refresh FIRST)\n9|\n10|This run opened on stale base `a12d1bd` (branch tip `47294bb`, the\n11|`TASK-260830-2g5be6` checkpoint) while the selected authority was trunk\n12|`c3aae73` — the exact shape that refused the previous attempt's CR\n13|construction (`change_request_base_authority_mismatch`). Per the brief,\n14|`task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-32ypr2` ran FIRST:\n15|\n16|- First attempt stopped for one regular-file conflict (`LOGBOOK.md`, replay\n17|  of `47294bb` onto `c3aae73`).\n18|- Resolution `--replay-resolutions /tmp/replay-resolutions.json`, binding\n19|  `checkpoint_oid 47294bb816429fa83e07e9889605201b35d7f045`,\n20|  `path LOGBOOK.md`,\n21|  `sha256 68ccfc48ccbecd0c915b0b2ce1e316f76816aa0ca0ca34bfb560489493a4a299`\n22|  (trunk's `STORY-260830-4qojoz` entry kept newest-first, the `2g5be6`\n23|  block carried verbatim below it, no marker left).\n24|- Outcome: `refresh_advanced`, `TrunkOID c3aae73…`, `BranchOID 3005d78…`.\n25|\n26|Post-refresh audit of `git diff --name-only a12d1bd c3aae73` against\n27|`git status`: the refresh had carried stale pre-refresh copies that read as\n28|reverts. Restored trunk bytes by hand for every non-owned path\n29|(`git checkout HEAD -- .task-board internal/matjournal internal/meshneg\n30|internal/rpcwire task-board.config.json` — the config is byte-identical to\n31|the new base, 30 commands, verified with `cmp`). Owned paths (LOGBOOK,\n32|README, the six `internal/traceability` files) were rebuilt purely\n33|additively on the NEW trunk bytes (details under Story-close); the\n34|untracked `internal/cloneproject/` package carried over untouched.\n35|`git status` at handoff shows only candidate paths.\n36|\n37|## Inherited work vs this run\n38|\n39|Inherited from the previous attempt (RUN-260918-6bd395, exit 0, CR refused\n40|on provenance only): the complete `internal/cloneproject` package\n41|(production + tests + TRACEABILITY.md + 45-row harness), the registry row\n42|content (4 cases, 7.8/10.2 full bindings), and the README/LOGBOOK/test-edit\n43|drafts — all written against the old base. This run verified every inherited\n44|claim firsthand instead of carrying it over:\n45|\n46|- Re-ran the package suite, both mutant batteries, tracecheck, and the full\n47|  30-command suite on the refreshed tree (all exits below are this run's).\n48|- Read every production file and the refusal/determinism/boundary proofs;\n49|  confirmed entry-point discipline (no test touches an unexported helper),\n50|  literal-token assertions (no production-constant expectations), landed\n51|  reuse (`len(text)` bytes vs the landed `len(text)` gate; `StringLength`\n52|  characters; digit-only uint53), and the real `clonesnap.Capture` fixture\n53|  path.\n54|- Strengthened the battery with 5 new rows (45 → 50): `N-protection-signed`,\n55|  `N-unknow