ed gate the plant narrows.\n20|Battery: 49 KILLED + control SURVIVED, executed twice, exit 0 both runs,\n21|one raw log per plant per run under `mutants/run1/` + `mutants/run2/` in the\n22|producer evidence archive.\n23|\n24|| # | AC behavior | Driving test(s) → call site | Narrowing(s) |\n25||---|---|---|---|\n26|| 1 | Wholly unknown native type → `opaque_event`, `opaque` visibility, `unknown_native_event` reason, identity kept | `TestNormalizeUnknownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` → `Normalize` → `dispatchRecord` default arm | `N-unknown-kind-wholly` (killer: admits exactly `frobnicate` into `user_message`) |\n27|| 2 | Almost-known record (right envelope, unknown inner type) never coerced into a neighbouring kind | `TestNormalizeAlmostKnownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` → same arm | `N-unknown-kind` (killer: admits exactly `message/smoke` into `user_message`) |\n28|| 3 | Unknown-class member → whole-member `opaque_event` (offset 0, full length, null native IDs) | `TestNormalizeUnknownMemberBecomesWholeMemberOpaque` → `Normalize` → `collectMembers` | `N-unknown-member` (killer: admits exactly `store/mystery` into JSONL parsing) |\n29|| 4 | Evidence ranges resolve to the exact captured bytes (manifest + descriptor linkage, in range) | `mustResolveRef` assertions in rows 1–3 tests + `mustResolveOverflow` in row 20 test; single-ref evidences asserted `len==1` (trivially sorted/unique) | `N-digest-verify`, `N-missing-blob` (fetch-integrity gates, killers on the refusal rows) |\n30|| 5 | Never dropped, guessed, or re-typed on a second projection | `TestNormalizeOpaqueIsStableAcrossProjections` (`Normalize` ×2 over fresh sinks, byte-equal, still `opaque_event`) | gate-level: rows 1–3 narrowings pin the kinds; structural: `Normalize` holds no cross-call state |\n31|| 6 | Foreign encrypted reasoning → `opaque_reasoning`, `foreign_encrypted_payload`, no content members, byte-exact round trip | `TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque` → `Normalize` → `dispatchProtected` | `N-protection-encrypted` (killer; token-preserving: the `encrypted` label still matches, the decision changes) |\n32|| 7 | Foreign signed reasoning → `opaque_reasoning`, `foreign_signature_unverifiable`, byte-exact | `TestNormalizeForeignSignedReasoningStaysOpaque` → same gate | `N-protection-signed` (killer: admits exactly `signed` past the gate) |\n33|| 8 | Never decrypted, re-encoded, summarized, truncated, or promoted; native-protected carries no foreign code; protected known content never semantic; unknown+protected carries both reasons | `TestNormalizeNativeProtectedReasoningStaysOpaque` + `TestNormalizeProtectedMessageBecomesOpaqueEvent` + `TestNormalizeUnknownProtectedRecordCarriesBothReasons` + forbidden-member sweeps (`content_blocks`, `content`, `text`, `ciphertext`, `summary` absent) in rows 6–7 tests | `N-native-reason-foreign` (killer), `N-reasons-both-single` (killer), `N-protection-encrypted` cross-kill on the protected-message test (verified by hand probe, `crosskill-encrypted-vs-protected-message.log`: exit 1 under the plant, `ok` restored) |\n34|| 9 | Foreign instructions are low-authority history: cannot change the effective snapshot or authority | `TestNormalizeForeignInstructionCannotChangeEffectiveSnapshot` + `TestNormalizeForeignOnlyInstructionLeavesSnapshotEmpty` → `foldInstructions` / `dispatchInstruction` | `N-foreign-instruction`, `N-foreign-payload-authority` (killers) |\n35|| 10 | Source usage never becomes target accounting | `TestNormalizeSourceUsageIsNotTargetAccounting` → `foldUsage` | `N-usage-target` (killer); `N-usage-number`, `N-usage-overflow` (value model) |\n36|| 11 | `tool_definition_snapshot` is history, `callable` false, never registers; live claims refuse | `TestNormalizeToolDefinitionNeverRegistersCallable` + refusal row `live_attestation_claim` → `dispatchDefinition` / `deriveLiveSurface` | `N-callable-false`, `N-callable` (killers) |\n37|| 12 | Call with result → `completed`, `internal` visibility, empty live surface | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_with_result` → `resolveToolCalls` / `dispatchCall` | `N-pending-completed` (killer) |\n38|| 13 | Call without result → `aborted`, `unsafe_pending_action`, blocks pending action | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_without_result` → same | `N-tool-incomplete`, `N-pending-aborted` (killers) |\n39|| 14 | Result without call → `aborted` orphan | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/result_without_call` → `resolveToolCalls` / `dispatchResult` | `N-tool-orphan` (killer) |\n40|| 15 | Result arriving after the capture boundary completes the same call | `TestNormalizeResultAfterBoundaryCompletes` (first capture `aborted`, second `completed`) → same pairing decision | gate-level: `N-tool-incomplete` (same `resolveToolCalls` decision; no dedicated plant) |\n41|| 16 | Nested/subagent call attributes to a parented subagent actor, never main | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/nested_subagent_call` → `checkActors` / `buildResult` | `N-subagent-actor` (killer) |\n42|| 17 | `internal` visibility and no pending action for every matrix row; live surface empty over mixed history | visibility assertions in every matrix subtest + `TestNormalizeLiveSurfaceStaysEmpty` → `deriveLiveSurface` | `N-pending-aborted`, `N-pending-completed`, `N-live-followup` (killers on the named rows) |\n43|| 18 | Canonical Event exact shape: contiguous ordinals from zero, predecessor parents, UUIDv7 actors, literal kinds/visibilities, landed re-decode of every sealed byte | `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` → `buildEvents` → `clonebundle.BuildCanonicalEvent` + `DecodeCanonicalEvent` | `N-parents-chain`, `N-native-type-token` (killers; token-preserving) |\n44|| 19 | Source Evidence `exact` status with stable reason codes | reason assertions in rows 1, 6, 7, 13 tests → `evidenceFor` | `N-reasons-both-single`, `N-native-reason-foreign` (killers) |\n45|| 20 | 64 KiB edge: 65536-byte text inline, 65537-byte text a byte-exact blob reference, never a truncation | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` → `contentBlockForText` / `installOverflow` | `N-overflow-bound`, `N-overflow-truncate` (killers) |\n46|| 21 | Canonical Session shape: main + referenced extras, ordinal-ordered unique IDs, last event as head, parent null only for main | `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` (incl. `ParentActorID == nil` for main) + row 16 subagent-parent assertion → `buildResult` → `clonebundle.BuildCanonicalSession` + decode | `N-main-parent` (killer: admits exactly main to the parented class; the landed builder refuses), `N-parents-chain` |\n47|| 22 | Determinism: same captured bytes → byte-identical session + events twice | `TestNormalizeIsDeterministic` (`Normalize` ×2 over fresh sinks, `bytes.Equal`) | none: a proven property, not a gate (sorted inputs, no clock; no plant required) |\n48|| 23 | Every refusal through `Normalize` naming the member, line, or blob | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable` (33 subtests) + `TestNormalizeRefusesUnstableCapture` + `TestNormalizeRefusesEnvironmentDrift` | one narrowing per family, each killing its row: `N-envelope-version`, `N-origin`, `N-protection-value`, `N-actor-selector`, `N-malformed-json`, `N-blank-line`, `N-body-member`, `N-instruction-authority`, `N-directive-count`, `N-definition-digest`, `N-usage-number`, `N-usage-overflow`, `N-duplicate-call`, `N-duplicate-result`, `N-live-followup`, `N-callable`, `N-actor-unmapped-fallback`, `N-actor-unreferenced`, `N-main-in-map`, `N-subagent-name`, `N-manifest-link`, `N-missing-blob`, `N-digest-verify`, `N-empty-projection`, `N-unstable`, `N-env-drift`, `N-string-bound`, `N-reasoning-contradiction` |\n49|| 24 | No partial bundle on failure; idempotent replay into a shared sink (byte-identical output, stable blob count) | `TestNormalizeFailureReturnsNoPartialBundle` + `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` | none: failure-injection proofs, not gates; crash semantics of the write itself owned by `internal/localstore` (landed fault suites) |\n50|\n51|Ratio: **24 of 24 AC rows driven** through the production entry by named\n52|committed tests. No row is prose-only.\n53|\n54|## B. Registry bindings claimed by this Story (tracecheck-measured)\n55|\n56|| Clause | Acceptance case → executing test(s) | Measured |\n57||---|---|---|\n58|| `7.8#1` large data by reference | `clone-projection-fidelity` → `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` | full 2/2, `--section 7.8` admitted |\n59|| `7.8#2` execution bindings equal fresh facts | `session-adapter-call-binding` → `TestCheckCallBinding`, `TestCheckCallBindingZeroFactsRefuse` (sessadapter owner) | full 2/2 |\n60|| `10.2#1` metadata in manifest | `clone-capture-contracts` → `TestBuildRawManifestRoundTrip`, `TestBuildCaptureManifestDerivesRawComplete`, `TestBuildCanonicalEventRoundTrip`, `TestRawManifestRefusals`, `TestCaptureManifestRefusals` | full 5/5, `--section 10.2` admitted |\n61|| `10.2#2` fsync + verify + atomic install | `clone-native-capture` → `TestCaptureSealsBothManifestsFromStoreBytes`, `TestCaptureInstallsEveryPayloadBlob`, `TestCaptureMultiChunkMember`, `TestCaptureLogRecordsDigestsOnly`, `TestCaptureRefusesOversizedMember`; plus `clone-projection-fidelity` → `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` | full 5/5 |\n62|| `10.2#3` digest-only metrics | `clone-native-capture` (same suite) | full 5/5 |\n63|| `10.2#4` chunk agreement | `clone-native-capture` (same suite) | full 5/5 |\n64|| `10.2#5` oversize refuses `capability_unavailable` | `clone-native-capture` (same suite) | full 5/5 |\n65|\n66|`section:13.14.1` is deliberately NOT BOUND in the registry: the section\n67|carries no RFC 2119 keyword line the `tracecheck` scanner can see (its\n68|obligations are closed-shape \"contains exactly\" sentences), so any binding\n69|would measure `unmeasured`, which assigned-scope admission deliberately\n70|refuses. The Story's 13.14.1 record is the three package `TRACEABILITY.md`\n71|files plus the three leaf matrices, executed by the three real suites bound\n72|above as `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`, and\n73|`clone-projection-fidelity`. This leaf's 13.14.1 rows are section C below.\n74|\n75|## C. Section 13.14.1 clause record (this leaf)\n76|\n77|Each row names the committed test that executes it through `Normalize`;\n78|full entry + note detail lives in `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`\n79|(Clause map), which this matrix incorporates.\n80|\n81|| Pinned clause | Test |\n82||---|---|\n83|| Unknown native records become raw-addressable opaque events | `TestNormalizeUnknownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` |\n84|| Almost-known records never coerced into a neighbouring kind | `TestNormalizeAlmostKnownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` |\n85|| Unknown-class members become whole-member opaque events | `TestNormalizeUnknownMemberBecomesWholeMemberOpaque` |\n86|| Opaque events never dropped, guessed, or re-typed | `TestNormalizeOpaqueIsStableAcrossProjections` |\n87|| Foreign encrypted reasoning is opaque-preserved | `TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque` |\n88|| Foreign signed reasoning is opaque-preserved | `TestNormalizeForeignSignedReasoningStaysOpaque` |\n89|| Native protected reasoning stays opaque with no foreign code | `TestNormalizeNativeProtectedReasoningStaysOpaque` |\n90|| Protected known content never reaches a semantic kind | `TestNormalizeProtectedMessageBecomesOpaqueEvent` |\n91|| Unknown+protected records carry both stable reasons | `TestNormalizeUnknownProtectedRecordCarriesBothReasons` |\n92|| Foreign instructions are low-authority history | `TestNormalizeForeignInstructionCannotChangeEffectiveSnapshot`, `TestNormalizeForeignOnlyInstructionLeavesSnapshotEmpty` |\n93|| Source usage is not target accounting | `TestNormalizeSourceUsageIsNotTargetAccounting` |\n94|| Historical tools inert; call+result resolves completed | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_with_result` |\n95|| Incomplete calls become aborted history and block pending action | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_without_result`, `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/result_without_call` |\n96|| Results arriving after the boundary complete the same call | `TestNormalizeResultAfterBoundaryCompletes` |\n97|| Nested calls attribute to a parented subagent actor | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/nested_subagent_call` |\n98|| Definitions never register a callable tool | `TestNormalizeToolDefinitionNeverRegistersCallable` |\n99|| Live surface stays empty over mixed history | `TestNormalizeLiveSurfaceStaysEmpty` |\n100|| Canonical Session bounds (actors, ordered event IDs, head) | `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` |\n101|| Inline content at most 64 KiB; oversized becomes a blob reference | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` |\n102|| Same captured bytes project byte-identical output | `TestNormalizeIsDeterministic` |\n103|| `unstable_archive` cannot enter target projection | `TestNormalizeRefusesUnstableCapture` |\n104|| Manifest link, blob fetch, digest/size agreement | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/manifest_closure_drift`, `/tampered_blob`, `/missing_blob` |\n105|| Framing-malformed records refuse with member+line named | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/malformed_json_line`, `/missing_envelope_member`, `/bad_envelope_version`, `/blank_line`, `/unknown_body_member`, `/contradictory_protection`, `/protected_plaintext_body`, `/invalid_utf8_line` |\n106|| Live claims by captured history refuse | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/live_attestation_claim`, `/live_followup_claim` |\n107|| Ambiguous tool pairings refuse | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/duplicate_call_id`, `/duplicate_result_id` |\n108|| Exact actor mapping (referenced iff mapped) | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/unmapped_actor`, `/unmapped_extra_actor`, `/main_actor_in_map` |\n109|| Instruction authority and usage value model | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_instruction_authority`, `/fractional_usage`, `/unsafe_usage_magnitude` |\n110|| Blob Descriptor reference resolves to installed bytes | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (`mustResolveOverflow`) |\n111|| Fsync + verify + atomic install before referencing | `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` |\n112|| Large data by reference, never embedded | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` |\n113|| String measure in characters | `TestNormalizeMultibyteStringMeasure`, `TestNormalizeRefusalTable` width rows |\n114|| Text is valid UTF-8, never rewritten | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/invalid_utf8_line` |\n115|\n116|## D. Stated bounds and NOT APPLICABLE (with owners)\n117|\n118|| Area | Status | Owner / evidence |\n119||---|---|---|\n120|| Fixture-native record envelope (`v`, `native_event_id`, `native_type`, `origin`, `protection`, `actor`, `body`) | Stated bound: test-defined framing, not a specification shape; body shapes exact, envelope extras unclaimed | this leaf (`doc.go`, `native.go` + refusal rows) |\n121|| Canonical kinds never emitted here (`session_started`, `approval_request`, `plan_update`, `progress`, `rate_limit`, `file_change`, `compaction`, `turn_*`, `subagent_*`, `error`, `migration_checkpoint`, `session_finished`) | NOT APPLICABLE: fact registries cover exactly the ten emitted kinds | normalization-sibling scope |\n122|| Non-text content blocks (`json`, `image`, `audio`, `document`, `resource_link`, `redacted`, `opaque`) | NOT APPLICABLE: this leaf seals `text` blocks only (inline or blob-referenced) | normalization-sibling scope; closed vocabulary enforced by the landed builder |\n123|| Capture statuses `partial`, `synthesized`, `unavailable` | NOT APPLICABLE: this leaf emits `exact` only | shape rules owned by the accepted `internal/clonebundle` suite |\n124|| Closed-shape internals (26-kind registry, 0..64 parents sorted-unique, UUIDv7, turn/time nullability, extensions, session scale bounds 1024/1M/1024) | Shape rules owned by the accepted `internal/clonebundle` suite; this leaf proves its output satisfies them by sealing + re-decoding every event and session (builder refusal = projection error) | `internal/clonebundle` (leaf 1, accepted) |\n125|| Actor UUIDv7 parsing | Gate owned by `internal/scalar`; entry refusal pinned by `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_actor_uuid` | `internal/scalar` (landed) |\n126|| `parent_actor_id` shape rule (null iff main) | Enforced by the landed builder; main-null asserted in `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape`, subagent-parent in `nested_subagent_call`, wiring narrowed by `N-main-parent` | `internal/clonebundle` builder + this leaf |\n127|| Closed core reason vocabulary (`unknown_native_event`, `foreign_encrypted_payload`, `foreign_signature_unverifiable`, `unsafe_pending_action`, …) | Referenced, not owned: defined by §13.14.2; this leaf emits four codes as evidence strings without implementing dispositions | §13.14.2 owner (sibling) |\n128|| §13.14.2 fidelity dispositions, projection planning, lineage | NOT APPLICABLE: sibling scope | §13.14.2 owner (sibling) |\n129|| §13.14.3 Migration Checkpoint / bundle chain | NOT APPLICABLE: sibling scope | §13.14.3 owner (sibling) |\n130|| §13.14.4 transaction / staging | NOT APPLICABLE: this Story plans no projection, stages no target | §13.14.4 owner (sibling) |\n131|| §13.14.5 tuple admission | NOT APPLICABLE: this Story admits no tuple | §13.14.5 owner (sibling) |\n132|| §7.8 operation frames (capture-plan/capture/normalize) | NOT APPLICABLE here: wiring stays `sessadapter`; this leaf owns the fidelity rules those operations must satisfy | `internal/sessadapter` (landed) |\n133|| Durable-write crash semantics (stage/fsync/verify/atomic install) | Owned by `internal/localstore` (landed fault suites); this leaf adds bundle atomicity (row 24) | `internal/localstore` (landed) |\n134|| `pending` live-work-order map parameter of `deriveLiveSurface` | Live-sibling API: `Normalize` always passes nil, so nothing captured can pend | live sibling (stated bound) |\n135|| `ax` command, `doctor` result, runtime capability | NOT CLAIMED anywhere in code, tests, README, or LOGBOOK | — |\n136|\n137|## E. Negative-evidence index\n138|\n139|Every refusal below is driven through `Normalize` over real captured bytes\n140|by the named committed test and reddened by the named narrowing (single\n141|member admitted). Production call sites: `Normalize` (`normalize.go`),\n142|`collectMembers` + `sealedEnvironment` (closure), `parseNativeLine` +\n143|`splitRecordLines` + body decoders (`native.go`), `dispatchRecord` /\n144|`dispatchProtected` (`dispatch.go`), `resolveToolCalls` + `deriveLiveSurface`\n145|(`tools.go`), `checkActors` + `buildEvents` + `buildResult` (`dispatch.go`).\n146|\n147|Refusal rows (33 in `TestNormalizeRefusalTable` + 2 standalone): see section\n148|A rows 11, 13, 17, 23 and section C. Token-preserving attacks:\n149|`N-native-type-token` (the `message/user` label still matches, routes to\n150|`assistant_message`; killer `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` executes the\n151|behavioral suite) and `N-protection-encrypted` (the `encrypted` label still\n152|matches, skips opaque dispatch; killer `TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque`).\n153|Harmless control: `C-doc-comment` (comment-only edit, SURVIVED exit 0 both\n154|runs), proving the harness observes outcomes instead of hard-coding kills.","final_result":true}}}
