{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c683","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3cf-5753-7b41-a2b3-ce03595a21fa"},"sequence":412,"recorded_at":1780531400000819,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3d0be3c760ea31d1d5366259668","text":"<read-skill-result name=\"go-testing-tools\" status=\"ok\">\n<metadata>\npath: /Users/iv/.agents/skills/go-testing-tools/SKILL.md\nlocator: file:///Users/iv/.agents/skills/go-testing-tools/SKILL.md\nsource: user\nbytes_returned: 15216\nbytes_total: 15216\ntruncated: false\n</metadata>\n\n<skill-body id=\"go-testing-tools\">\n---\nname: go-testing-tools\ndescription: &gt;\n  Go testing toolkit with tuitestkit library and a closed-loop development\n  cycle for Go applications. Covers test helpers, reducer tests,\n  snapshot/golden testing, mock executor patterns, and view assertions.\ntriggers:\n  - go test\n  - bubbletea test\n  - tuitestkit\n  - go test helpers\n  - reducer test\n  - snapshot test go\n  - golden file go\n  - тесты го\n  - го тест хелперы\n  - тесты баблти\n  - тест утилиты го\n  - замкнутый цикл тестирования\n---\n\n# Go Testing Tools\n\nTesting toolkit for Go TUI applications built with bubbletea. Provides a Go library (`tuitestkit`), reference documentation, and templates that enable a closed-loop development cycle: write code, write tests, run tests, validate, fix, repeat -- all without human intervention.\n\nCore philosophy: **Elm architecture makes TUI testable.** The reducer is a pure function -- given the same state and action, it always returns the same result. No I/O, no randomness, no terminal. Test everything as function calls.\n\n---\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- **Go 1.21+**\n- **bubbletea** (`github.com/charmbracelet/bubbletea`)\n- **lipgloss** (`github.com/charmbracelet/lipgloss`) -- used by most bubbletea apps for styling\n\nInstall the library in your project:\n\n```bash\ngo get github.com/relux-works/skill-go-testing-tools/tuitestkit\n```\n\n---\n\n## Quick Start\n\nMinimal test showing the core workflow: build a message, send it to a model, assert on the view.\n\n```go\npackage myscreen_test\n\nimport (\n    &quot;testing&quot;\n\n    &quot;github.com/relux-works/skill-go-testing-tools/tuitestkit&quot;\n)\n\nfunc TestBasicNavigation(t *testing.T) {\n    m := NewMyModel(testData)\n    m = tuitestkit.Send(m, tuitestkit.WindowSize(80, 24))\n\n    // Press down twice\n    m = tuitestkit.Send(m, tuitestkit.Key(&quot;down&quot;), tuitestkit.Key(&quot;down&quot;))\n\n    // Assert the view contains expected content\n    tuitestkit.ViewContains(t, m, &quot;third item&quot;)\n    tuitestkit.ViewNotContains(t, m, &quot;ERROR&quot;)\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## Testing Pyramid\n\nFive levels, from fastest/most numerous to slowest/fewest:\n\n| Level | What | Speed | Investment |\n|-------|------|-------|------------|\n| 1. Pure Reducer | `func(State, Action) State` | Nanoseconds | ~60% |\n| 2. Component | `Update` + `View` | Microseconds | ~20% |\n| 3. Integration | Multi-component with mocks | Milliseconds | ~10% |\n| 4. Snapshot | Golden file comparison | Milliseconds | ~5% |\n| 5. Behavioral | Full user workflows | Milliseconds | ~5% |\n\nWhen time is limited: **Level 1 &gt; Level 2 &gt; Level 3**. Pure reducer tests catch the most bugs per line of test code.\n\nFull details: `references/testing-pyramid.md`\n\n---\n\n## Library API Reference\n\nAll functions are in the `tuitestkit` package.\n\n### Message Builders (`messages.go`)\n\nBuild `tea.Msg` values for driving model updates.\n\n```go\n// Key builds a tea.KeyMsg from a human-readable string.\n// Supports: &quot;enter&quot;, &quot;tab&quot;, &quot;esc&quot;, &quot;space&quot;, &quot;backspace&quot;, &quot;up&quot;, &quot;down&quot;,\n// &quot;left&quot;, &quot;right&quot;, &quot;home&quot;, &quot;end&quot;, &quot;pgup&quot;, &quot;pgdown&quot;, &quot;delete&quot;, &quot;insert&quot;,\n// &quot;f1&quot;-&quot;f20&quot;, &quot;ctrl+c&quot;, &quot;ctrl+a&quot;...&quot;ctrl+z&quot;, &quot;alt+h&quot;, &quot;alt+enter&quot;,\n// single runes: &quot;a&quot;, &quot;/&quot;, &quot;1&quot;, etc.\nfunc Key(k string) tea.KeyMsg\n\n// Keys builds a slice of tea.Msg from multiple key strings.\nfunc Keys(keys ...string) []tea.Msg\n\n// WindowSize builds a tea.WindowSizeMsg with the given dimensions.\nfunc WindowSize(w, h int) tea.WindowSizeMsg\n\n// MouseClick builds a tea.MouseMsg for a left-button click at (x, y).\nfunc MouseClick(x, y int) tea.MouseMsg\n\n// MouseClickRight builds a tea.MouseMsg for a right-button click at (x, y).\nfunc MouseClickRight(x, y int) tea.MouseMsg\n\n// MouseScroll builds a tea.MouseMsg for a scroll event.\n// Direction constants: ScrollUp, ScrollDown, ScrollLeft, ScrollRight.\nfunc MouseScroll(dir ScrollDir) tea.MouseMsg\n\n// MouseRelease builds a tea.MouseMsg for a button release at (x, y).\nfunc MouseRelease(x, y int) tea.MouseMsg\n```\n\n### Model Harness (`harness.go`)\n\nSend messages to bubbletea models and handle commands.\n\n```go\n// Send sends messages to a model sequentially, returns the final model.\n// Preserves concrete type via generics -- no type assertion needed.\n// Panics if Update returns a different type (broken implementation).\n// Init() is NOT called.\nfunc Send[M tea.Model](model M, msgs ...tea.Msg) M\n\n// SendAndCollect sends messages, collects all non-nil Cmds returned by Update.\n// Returns final model + collected commands.\nfunc SendAndCollect[M tea.Model](model M, msgs ...tea.Msg) (M, []tea.Cmd)\n\n// ExecCmds executes tea.Cmd functions synchronously, collects resulting messages.\n// Recursively handles tea.BatchMsg. Nil cmds/messages are skipped.\nfunc ExecCmds(cmds ...tea.Cmd) []tea.Msg\n```\n\n**Common pattern -- command pipeline:**\n\n```go\nm, cmds := tuitestkit.SendAndCollect(m, tuitestkit.Key(&quot;r&quot;))\nmsgs := tuitestkit.ExecCmds(cmds...)\nm = tuitestkit.Send(m, msgs...)\n```\n\n### Reducer Harness (`reducer.go`)\n\nTable-driven testing for pure reducer functions.\n\n```go\n// ReducerTest defines a single test case for a pure reducer.\n// S = state type, A = action type.\ntype ReducerTest[S any, A any] struct {\n    Name    string\n    Initial S\n    Action  A\n    Assert  func(t *testing.T, got S)\n}\n\n// Step defines one step in a multi-action reducer sequence.\n// Assert is optional -- if nil, applied without per-step validation.\ntype Step[S any, A any] struct {\n    Name   string\n    Action A\n    Assert func(t *testing.T, got S)\n}\n\n// ReducerSequence defines a multi-step test scenario.\n// Actions applied sequentially from Initial. Final runs on end state.\ntype ReducerSequence[S, A any] struct {\n    Name    string\n    Initial S\n    Steps   []Step[S, A]\n    Final   func(t *testing.T, got S)\n}\n\n// RunReducerTests executes table-driven reducer tests as subtests.\nfunc RunReducerTests[S, A any](t *testing.T, reduce func(S, A) S, tests []ReducerTest[S, A])\n\n// RunReducerSequences executes multi-step sequence tests.\n// Per-step Assert runs after each step (if non-nil). Final runs on end state.\nfunc RunReducerSequences[S, A any](t *testing.T, reduce func(S, A) S, sequences []ReducerSequence[S, A])\n```\n\n**Invariant checking:**\n\n```go\n// Invariant defines a property that must hold for any state.\ntype Invariant[S any] struct {\n    Name  string\n    Check func(s S) error\n}\n\n// InvariantChecker holds invariants and validates state against all of them.\ntype InvariantChecker[S any] struct { /* ... */ }\n\n// NewInvariantChecker creates a checker with the given invariants.\nfunc NewInvariantChecker[S any](invariants ...Invariant[S]) *InvariantChecker[S]\n\n// Check validates state against all invariants. Returns combined error or nil.\nfunc (ic *InvariantChecker[S]) Check(s S) error\n\n// WrapWithInvariants wraps a reducer with invariant checking.\n// After every reduce call, all invariants are validated.\n// t.Fatalf on violation.\nfunc WrapWithInvariants[S, A any](t *testing.T, reduce func(S, A) S, checker *InvariantChecker[S]) func(S, A) S\n```\n\n**Example:**\n\n```go\nchecker := tuitestkit.NewInvariantChecker(\n    tuitestkit.Invariant[AppState]{\n        Name: &quot;cursor in bounds&quot;,\n        Check: func(s AppState) error {\n            if s.Cursor &lt; 0 || s.Cursor &gt;= len(s.Items) {\n                return fmt.Errorf(&quot;cursor %d out of [0, %d)&quot;, s.Cursor, len(s.Items))\n            }\n            return nil\n        },\n    },\n)\nsafeReduce := tuitestkit.WrapWithInvariants(t, Reduce, checker)\ntuitestkit.RunReducerTests(t, safeReduce, tests)\n```\n\n### Mock Building Blocks (`mock.go`)\n\nComposable primitives for building project-specific mocks.\n\n```go\n// MockCall represents a single recorded method invocation.\ntype MockCall struct {\n    Method string\n    Args   []any\n}\n\n// MockCallRecorder provides thread-safe recording of method calls.\n// Embed into project-specific mock structs.\ntype MockCallRecorder struct { /* ... */ }\n\nfunc (r *MockCallRecorder) Record(method string, args ...any)\nfunc (r *MockCallRecorder) CallCount(method string) int\nfunc (r *MockCallRecorder) Calls() []MockCall\nfunc (r *MockCallRecorder) CallsFor(method string) []MockCall\nfunc (r *MockCallRecorder) Reset()\n\n// MockResponseMap provides thread-safe canned response storage.\ntype MockResponseMap struct { /* ... */ }\n\nfunc NewMockResponseMap() *MockResponseMap\nfunc (m *MockResponseMap) Set(key string, data []byte, err error)\nfunc (m *MockResponseMap) Get(key string) ([]byte, error)\nfunc (m *MockResponseMap) SetError(key string, err error)\n\n// Assertion helpers\nfunc AssertCalled(t testing.TB, r *MockCallRecorder, method string)\nfunc AssertNotCalled(t testing.TB, r *MockCallRecorder, method string)\nfunc AssertCalledN(t testing.TB, r *MockCallRecorder, method string, n int)\nfunc AssertCalledWith(t testing.TB, r *MockCallRecorder, method string, args ...any)\n```\n\n**Building a mock (two lines per method):**\n\n```go\ntype TaskBoardMock struct {\n    tuitestkit.MockCallRecorder\n    Responses *tuitestkit.MockResponseMap\n}\n\nfunc NewTaskBoardMock() *TaskBoardMock {\n    return &amp;TaskBoardMock{Responses: tuitestkit.NewMockResponseMap()}\n}\n\nfunc (m *TaskBoardMock) TreeJSON() ([]byte, error) {\n    m.Record(&quot;TreeJSON&quot;)\n    return m.Responses.Get(&quot;TreeJSON&quot;)\n}\n\nfunc (m *TaskBoardMock) Execute(cmd string, args ...string) ([]byte, error) {\n    m.Record(&quot;Execute&quot;, cmd, args)\n    return m.Responses.Get(&quot;Execute:&quot; + cmd)\n}\n```\n\n### View Assertions (`view.go`)\n\nAssert on rendered output. All functions strip ANSI escape codes before comparison.\n\n```go\n// StripANSI removes all ANSI escape sequences from a string.\nfunc StripANSI(s string) string\n\n// --- Model-based (call model.View() internally) ---\n\nfunc ViewContains(t testing.TB, model tea.Model, text string)\nfunc ViewNotContains(t testing.TB, model tea.Model, text string)\nfunc ViewLines(model tea.Model) []string\nfunc ViewLineContains(t testing.TB, model tea.Model, lineIdx int, text string)\nfunc ViewLineEquals(t testing.TB, model tea.Model, lineIdx int, text string)\nfunc ViewMatchesRegex(t testing.TB, model tea.Model, pattern string)\n\n// --- String-based (when you already have the view string) ---\n\nfunc ContainsStr(t testing.TB, view string, text string)\nfunc NotContainsStr(t testing.TB, view string, text string)\nfunc LinesFromStr(view string) []string\nfunc MatchesRegexStr(t testing.TB, view string, pattern string)\n```\n\n### Snapshot Testing (`snapshot.go`)\n\nGolden file comparison for visual regression testing.\n\n```go\n// UpdateSnapshots controls whether snapshots are written (true) or compared (false).\n// Set via UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1 environment variable.\nvar UpdateSnapshots bool\n\n// SnapshotView captures model.View(), strips ANSI, compares against golden file.\nfunc SnapshotView(t *testing.T, model tea.Model, name string)\n\n// SnapshotViewRaw captures model.View() with raw ANSI codes intact.\nfunc SnapshotViewRaw(t *testing.T, model tea.Model, name string)\n\n// SnapshotStr compares a pre-rendered string (ANSI-stripped) against golden file.\nfunc SnapshotStr(t *testing.T, view string, name string)\n\n// SnapshotStrRaw compares a pre-rendered string (raw ANSI) against golden file.\nfunc SnapshotStrRaw(t *testing.T, view string, name string)\n```\n\nGolden files stored at `testdata/snapshots/&lt;name&gt;.golden` relative to the test file.\n\n```bash\n# Create or update golden files\nUPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1 go test ./...\n\n# Update for a single package\nUPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1 go test ./internal/ui/screens/board/ -run TestSnapshot\n```\n\nMismatches produce a line-by-line diff with `-`/`+` markers.\n\n---\n\n## Closed-Loop Workflow\n\nThe agent development cycle for writing tests:\n\n```\n1. UNDERSTAND: Read screen/component code\n2. IDENTIFY:   What behaviors need tests?\n3. EXTRACT:    If exec.Command present, extract to interface (use mock template)\n4. WRITE:      Tests using tuitestkit helpers\n5. RUN:        go test ./... -v\n6. VALIDATE:   All pass? Check coverage with go test -cover\n7. FIX:        If failures, read error, fix code or test, goto 5\n8. SNAPSHOT:   Optionally capture view golden files\n9. DONE:       Tests green, coverage acceptable\n```\n\n### Step Details\n\n**UNDERSTAND:** Read the component source. Identify:\n- What state does it manage?\n- What messages does it handle in Update?\n- Does it have a pure reducer (`func(State, Action) State`)?\n- Does it shell out to external commands (exec.Command)?\n- What does View() render?\n\n**IDENTIFY:** Map behaviors to test levels:\n- Pure state logic -&gt; Level 1 (reducer tests)\n- Key bindings, view rendering -&gt; Level 2 (component tests)\n- Data loading, command execution -&gt; Level 3 (integration tests with mocks)\n- Visual appearance -&gt; Level 4 (snapshot tests)\n\n**EXTRACT:** If the component uses `exec.Command` or any I/O directly:\n1. Define an interface with only the methods this component needs\n2. Move `exec.Command` calls to a production implementation\n3. Build a mock using `MockCallRecorder` + `MockResponseMap`\n4. See `assets/templates/executor_interface.go.tmpl` and `assets/templates/mock_executor.go.tmpl`\n\n**WRITE:** Use the appropriate tuitestkit helpers per level:\n- Level 1: `RunReducerTests`, `RunReducerSequences`, `WrapWithInvariants`\n- Level 2: `Send`, `ViewContains`, `ViewLines`, `Key`, `MouseClick`\n- Level 3: `SendAndCollect`, `ExecCmds`, `AssertCalled`, `AssertCalledWith`\n- Level 4: `SnapshotView`, `SnapshotStr`\n\n**RUN:** `go test ./... -v` -- all tests must run in under 1 second (no I/O, no network).\n\n**VALIDATE:** `go test ./... -cover` -- target 80%+ for code under test.\n\n**FIX:** Read error messages carefully. Common issues:\n- Type assertion panic -&gt; `Update` returns wrong type (broken implementation)\n- View assertion failure -&gt; check ANSI stripping, check exact text\n- Snapshot mismatch -&gt; run with `UPDATE_SNAPSHOTS=1` if the change is intentional\n- Mock assertion failure -&gt; check response key matches (`&quot;Execute:list&quot;` not `&quot;Execute&quot;`)\n\n---\n\n## Templates\n\nScaffolding templates in `assets/templates/`:\n\n| Template | Purpose |\n|----------|---------|\n| `reducer_test.go.tmpl` | Table-driven reducer tests with invariants |\n| `component_test.go.tmpl` | Component model tests (keyboard, mouse, commands, view) |\n| `snapshot_test.go.tmpl` | Snapshot golden file tests |\n| `executor_interface.go.tmpl` | Executor interface + production stub |\n| `mock_executor.go.tmpl` | Mock executor using MockCallRecorder + MockResponseMap |\n| `PROJECT_STRUCTURE.md` | Recommended directory layout for test files |\n\nCopy templates into your project, replace `TODO` markers with your actual types and import paths.\n\n---\n\n## References\n\nIn-depth documentation in `references/`:\n\n| Document | Content |\n|----------|---------|\n| `elm-architecture.md` | Why Elm makes TUI testable, state/action/reducer/view cycle, nested reducers, dependency injection, the executor pattern |\n| `mock-patterns.md` | Interface extraction, when to mock vs test pure functions, stubs vs mocks vs fakes, callback capture, full mock lifecycle example |\n| `testing-pyramid.md` | All 5 test levels with code examples, decision table for which level to use, coverage strategy |\n\n---\n\n## Setup\n\nRun the setup script to create symlinks:\n\n```bash\n./scripts/setup.sh\n```\n\nThis links the skill to `~/.agents/skills/go-testing-tools`, `~/.claude/skills/go-testing-tools`, and `~/.codex/skills/go-testing-tools`.\n\nTo remove:\n\n```bash\n./scripts/deinit.sh\n```\n\n</skill-body>\n</read-skill-result>","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_skill","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c685","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3cf-5753-7b41-a2b3-ce03595a21fa"},"sequence":413,"recorded_at":1780531400000821,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3d0bfd874149925f8ae270848e3","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree/internal/cloneproject/native.go`.\n1|package cloneproject\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"bytes\"\n5|\t\"encoding/json\"\n6|\t\"strconv\"\n7|\t\"strings\"\n8|\t\"unicode/utf8\"\n9|\n10|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/environ\"\n11|)\n12|\n13|// This file parses the fixture-native record envelope. The envelope\n14|// is test-defined framing, not a specification shape: its only job\n15|// is to carry attributable bytes (native ID, native type, origin,\n16|// protection, actor, body) from captured members to the projection.\n17|// Every per-kind body shape below is exact: unknown body members\n18|// refuse rather than silently drop, so a projection can never claim\n19|// a faithful kind while ignoring a fact it does not understand. Type\n20|// level unknowns become opaque_event; field level unknowns inside a\n21|// known type refuse (see doc.go).\n22|\n23|// NativeRecord is one parsed fixture-native record with its byte\n24|// range inside the member blob.\n25|type NativeRecord struct {\n26|\t// MemberKey is the capture native item key holding the record.\n27|\tMemberKey string\n28|\t// Line is the one-based line number inside the member.\n29|\tLine int\n30|\t// Offset and Length are the record's byte range: the line\n31|\t// without its newline terminator.\n32|\tOffset uint64\n33|\tLength uint64\n34|\t// NativeEventID and NativeType attribute the record.\n35|\tNativeEventID string\n36|\tNativeType    string\n37|\t// Origin is native or foreign.\n38|\tOrigin string\n39|\t// Protection is none, encrypted, or signed.\n40|\tProtection string\n41|\t// Actor is main, external, or subagent:<name>.\n42|\tActor string\n43|\t// Body carries the raw body value; kind code reads only its\n44|\t// registered members.\n45|\tBody json.RawMessage\n46|\t// LineBytes are the exact record bytes preserved for opaque kinds.\n47|\tLineBytes []byte\n48|}\n49|\n50|// nativeEnvelope is the decoded envelope shape. Body stays raw:\n51|// each known type validates its own exact members.\n52|type nativeEnvelope struct {\n53|\tVersion       json.Number     `json:\"v\"`\n54|\tNativeEventID string          `json:\"native_event_id\"`\n55|\tNativeType    string          `json:\"native_type\"`\n56|\tOrigin        string          `json:\"origin\"`\n57|\tProtection    string          `json:\"protection\"`\n58|\tActor         string          `json:\"actor\"`\n59|\tBody          json.RawMessage `json:\"body\"`\n60|}\n61|\n62|// parseNativeLine parses one record line. A line that is not valid\n63|// UTF-8, not a JSON object, or misses an envelope member refuses\n64|// with the member and line named: malformed framing is an error,\n65|// never an absent or guessed record.\n66|func parseNativeLine(memberKey string, line int, offset uint64, raw []byte) (NativeRecord, error) {\n67|\twhere := func() string {\n68|\t\treturn \"record \" + memberKey + \" line \" + itoa(line)\n69|\t}\n70|\tif !utf8.Valid(raw) {\n71|\t\treturn NativeRecord{}, invalid(\"%s is not valid UTF-8\", where())\n72|\t}\n73|\tdecoder := json.NewDecoder(bytes.NewReader(raw))\n74|\tdecoder.UseNumber()\n75|\tvar members map[string]json.RawMessage\n76|\tif err := decoder.Decode(&members); err != nil {\n77|\t\treturn NativeRecord{}, invalid(\"%s is not a JSON object: %v\", where(), err)\n78|\t}\n79|\tif decoder.More() {\n80|\t\treturn NativeRecord{}, invalid(\"%s carries trailing bytes\", where())\n81|\t}\n82|\tfor _, name := range []string{\"v\", \"native_event_id\", \"native_type\", \"origin\", \"protection\", \"actor\", \"body\"} {\n83|\t\tif _, ok := members[name]; !ok {\n84|\t\t\treturn NativeRecord{}, invalid(\"%s misses envelope member %q\", where(), name)\n85|\t\t}\n86|\t}\n87|\tvar envelope nativeEnvelope\n88|\tstrict := json.NewDecoder(bytes.NewReader(raw))\n89|\tstrict.UseNumber()\n90|\tif err := strict.Decode(&envelope); err != nil {\n91|\t\treturn NativeRecord{}, invalid(\"%s is not a JSON object: %v\", where(), err)\n92|\t}\n93|\tif envelope.Version.String() != \"1\" {\n94|\t\treturn NativeRecord{}, invalid(\"%s carries envelope version %q, want 1\", where(), envelope.Version.String())\n95|\t}\n96|\tif environ.StringLength(envelope.NativeEventID) < 1 || environ.StringLength(envelope.NativeEventID) > 512 {\n97|\t\treturn NativeRecord{}, invalid(\"%s native_event_id is not a string[1..512]\", where())\n98|\t}\n99|\tif environ.StringLength(envelope.NativeType) < 1 || environ.StringLength(envelope.NativeType) > 512 {\n100|\t\treturn NativeRecord{}, invalid(\"%s native_type is not a string[1..512]\", where())\n101|\t}\n102|\tif envelope.Origin != \"native\" && envelope.Origin != \"foreign\" {\n103|\t\treturn NativeRecord{}, invalid(\"%s origin %q is outside native|foreign\", where(), envelope.Origin)\n104|\t}\n105|\tif envelope.Protection != \"none\" && envelope.Protection != \"encrypted\" && envelope.Protection != \"signed\" {\n106|\t\treturn NativeRecord{}, invalid(\"%s protection %q is outside none|encrypted|signed\", where(), envelope.Protection)\n107|\t}\n108|\tif err := checkActorSelector(envelope.Actor); err != nil {\n109|\t\treturn NativeRecord{}, invalid(\"%s %v\", where(), err)\n110|\t}\n111|\treturn NativeRecord{\n112|\t\tMemberKey:     memberKey,\n113|\t\tLine:          line,\n114|\t\tOffset:        offset,\n115|\t\tLength:        uint64(len(raw)),\n116|\t\tNativeEventID: envelope.NativeEventID,\n117|\t\tNativeType:    envelope.NativeType,\n118|\t\tOrigin:        envelope.Origin,\n119|\t\tProtection:    envelope.Protection,\n120|\t\tActor:         envelope.Actor,\n121|\t\tBody:          envelope.Body,\n122|\t\tLineBytes:     append([]byte(nil), raw...),\n123|\t}, nil\n124|}\n125|\n126|// checkActorSelector validates main, external, or subagent:<name>\n127|// with a bounded non-empty name.\n128|func checkActorSelector(selector string) error {\n129|\tif selector == \"main\" || selector == \"external\" {\n130|\t\treturn nil\n131|\t}\n132|\tname, ok := strings.CutPrefix(selector, \"subagent:\")\n133|\tif !ok || name == \"\" {\n134|\t\treturn invalid(\"actor %q is outside main|external|subagent:<name>\", selector)\n135|\t}\n136|\tif environ.StringLength(name) > 128 {\n137|\t\treturn invalid(\"actor %q names a subagent past 128 characters\", selector)\n138|\t}\n139|\treturn nil\n140|}\n141|\n142|// splitRecordLines splits member bytes into record lines with byte\n143|// offsets. A zero-byte member holds zero records; otherwise one\n144|// trailing newline is the terminator and every remaining line must\n145|// be non-empty: a blank line is malformed framing, never an absent\n146|// record.\n147|func splitRecordLines(memberKey string, payload []byte) ([]recordLine, error) {\n148|\tif len(payload) == 0 {\n149|\t\treturn nil, nil\n150|\t}\n151|\trest := payload\n152|\tif rest[len(rest)-1] == '\\n' {\n153|\t\trest = rest[:len(rest)-1]\n154|\t}\n155|\tvar lines []recordLine\n156|\toffset := uint64(0)\n157|\tnumber := 1\n158|\tfor {\n159|\t\tend := bytes.IndexByte(rest, '\\n')\n160|\t\tvar raw []byte\n161|\t\tif end < 0 {\n162|\t\t\traw = rest\n163|\t\t\trest = nil\n164|\t\t} else {\n165|\t\t\traw = rest[:end]\n166|\t\t\trest = rest[end+1:]\n167|\t\t}\n168|\t\tif len(raw) == 0 {\n169|\t\t\treturn nil, invalid(\"record %s line %d is empty\", memberKey, number)\n170|\t\t}\n171|\t\tlines = append(lines, recordLine{number: number, offset: offset, raw: raw})\n172|\t\toffset += uint64(len(raw)) + 1\n173|\t\tnumber++\n174|\t\tif rest == nil {\n175|\t\t\tbreak\n176|\t\t}\n177|\t}\n178|\treturn lines, nil\n179|}\n180|\n181|// recordLine is one split line with its number and byte offset.\n182|type recordLine struct {\n183|\tnumber int\n184|\toffset uint64\n185|\traw    []byte\n186|}\n187|\n188|// itoa renders a line number for refusal messages.\n189|func itoa(value int) string {\n190|\treturn strconv.Itoa(value)\n191|}\n192|\n193|// Known fixture-native types. Every other native_type projects as\n194|// opaque_event.\n195|const (\n196|\tnativeMessageUser      = \"message/user\"\n197|\tnativeMessageAssistant = \"message/assistant\"\n198|\tnativeReasoningSummary = \"reasoning/summary\"\n199|\tnativeReasoningCrypt   = \"reasoning/encrypted\"\n200|\tnativeReasoningSigned  = \"reasoning/signed\"\n201|\tnativeInstruction      = \"instruction/snapshot\"\n202|\tnativeToolDefinition   = \"tool/definition\"\n203|\tnativeToolCall         = \"tool/call\"\n204|\tnativeToolResult       = \"tool/result\"\n205|\tnativeUsage            = \"usage/report\"\n206|)\n207|\n208|// knownNativeType reports whether the native type selects a\n209|// registered projection. Unknown types become opaque_event.\n210|func knownNativeType(nativeType string) bool {\n211|\tswitch nativeType {\n212|\tcase nativeMessageUser,\n213|\t\tnativeMessageAssistant,\n214|\t\tnativeReasoningSummary,\n215|\t\tnativeReasoningCrypt,\n216|\t\tnativeReasoningSigned,\n217|\t\tnativeInstruction,\n218|\t\tnativeToolDefinition,\n219|\t\tnativeToolCall,\n220|\t\tnativeToolResult,\n221|\t\tnativeUsage:\n222|\t\treturn true\n223|\tdefault:\n224|\t\treturn false\n225|\t}\n226|}\n227|\n228|// decodeBodyObject decodes a body object with exact members: every\n229|// member must be registered for the type, and every required member\n230|// must be present. Unknown members refuse.\n231|func decodeBodyObject(record NativeRecord, required []string, allowed map[string]bool) (map[string]json.RawMessage, error) {\n232|\twhere := \"record \" + record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(record.Line)\n233|\tdecoder := json.NewDecoder(bytes.NewReader(bytes.TrimSpace(record.Body)))\n234|\tdecoder.UseNumber()\n235|\tvar members map[string]json.RawMessage\n236|\tif err := decoder.Decode(&members); err != nil {\n237|\t\treturn nil, invalid(\"%s body is not a JSON object: %v\", where, err)\n238|\t}\n239|\tfor name := range members {\n240|\t\tif !allowed[name] {\n241|\t\t\treturn nil, invalid(\"%s body carries unknown member %q\", where, name)\n242|\t\t}\n243|\t}\n244|\tfor _, name := range required {\n245|\t\tif _, ok := members[name]; !ok {\n246|\t\t\treturn nil, invalid(\"%s body misses member %q\", where, name)\n247|\t\t}\n248|\t}\n249|\treturn members, nil\n250|}\n251|\n252|// bodyString reads one required string body member.\n253|func bodyString(record NativeRecord, members map[string]json.RawMessage, name string) (string, error) {\n254|\twhere := \"record \" + record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(record.Line)\n255|\tvar value string\n256|\tif err := json.Unmarshal(members[name], &value); err != nil {\n257|\t\treturn \"\", invalid(\"%s body member %q is not a string\", where, name)\n258|\t}\n259|\treturn value, nil\n260|}\n261|\n262|// bodyOptionalBool reads one optional boolean body member.\n263|func bodyOptionalBool(record NativeRecord, members map[string]json.RawMessage, name string) (bool, error) {\n264|\twhere := \"record \" + record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(record.Line)\n265|\traw, ok := members[name]\n266|\tif !ok {\n267|\t\treturn false, nil\n268|\t}\n269|\tvar value bool\n270|\tif err := json.Unmarshal(raw, &value); err != nil {\n271|\t\treturn false, invalid(\"%s body member %q is not a boolean\", where, name)\n272|\t}\n273|\treturn value, nil\n274|}\n275|\n276|// bodyUint53 reads one required uint53 body member: an integer\n277|// literal in [0..2^53-1], never a fraction, exponent, or string.\n278|func bodyUint53(record NativeRecord, members map[string]json.RawMessage, name string) (uint64, error) {\n279|\twhere := \"record \" + record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(record.Line)\n280|\tdecoder := json.NewDecoder(bytes.NewReader(members[name]))\n281|\tdecoder.UseNumber()\n282|\tvar value json.Number\n283|\tif err := decoder.Decode(&value); err != nil {\n284|\t\treturn 0, invalid(\"%s body member %q is not a number\", where, name)\n285|\t}\n286|\ttext := value.String()\n287|\tif len(text) == 0 {\n288|\t\treturn 0, invalid(\"%s body member %q is not a uint53\", where, name)\n289|\t}\n290|\tfor i := 0; i < len(text); i++ {\n291|\t\tif text[i] < '0' || text[i] > '9' {\n292|\t\t\treturn 0, invalid(\"%s body member %q is not a uint53\", where, name)\n293|\t\t}\n294|\t}\n295|\tparsed, err := strconv.ParseUint(text, 10, 53)\n296|\tif err != nil {\n297|\t\treturn 0, invalid(\"%s body member %q exceeds uint53\", where, name)\n298|\t}\n299|\treturn parsed, nil\n300|}\n301|\n302|// maxUint53 is 2^53-1, the AX safe-integer ceiling.\n303|const maxUint53 = uint64(1<<53 - 1)\n304|\n305|// messageBody is the exact message/reasoning-summary body: text only.\n306|type messageBody struct {\n307|\tText string\n308|}\n309|\n310|// decodeMessageBody validates the exact {\"text\"} body.\n311|func decodeMessageBody(record NativeRecord) (messageBody, error) {\n312|\tmembers, err := decodeBodyObject(record, []string{\"text\"}, map[string]bool{\"text\": true})\n313|\tif err != nil {\n314|\t\treturn messageBody{}, err\n315|\t}\n316|\ttext, err := bodyString(record, members, \"text\")\n317|\tif err != nil {\n318|\t\treturn messageBody{}, err\n319|\t}\n320|\treturn messageBody{Text: text}, nil\n321|}\n322|\n323|// protectedBody is the exact protected-reasoning body: ciphertext\n324|// the projection never reads, only preserves byte-exact.\n325|type protectedBody struct {\n326|\tCiphertext string\n327|}\n328|\n329|// decodeProtectedBody validates the exact {\"ciphertext\"} body. The\n330|// value is framing-checked as a string and never interpreted.\n331|func decodeProtectedBody(record NativeRecord) (protectedBody, error) {\n332|\tmembers, err := decodeBodyObject(record, []string{\"ciphertext\"}, map[string]bool{\"ciphertext\": true})\n333|\tif err != nil {\n334|\t\treturn protectedBody{}, err\n335|\t}\n336|\tciphertext, err := bodyString(record, members, \"ciphertext\")\n337|\tif err != nil {\n338|\t\treturn protectedBody{}, err\n339|\t}\n340|\treturn protectedBody{Ciphertext: ciphertext}, nil\n341|}\n342|\n343|// instructionBody is the exact instruction-snapshot body.\n344|type instructionBody struct {\n345|\tAuthority  string\n346|\tDirectives []string\n347|}\n348|\n349|// decodeInstructionBody validates authority high|low and up to 1024\n350|// directives of 1..4096 characters each.\n351|func decodeInstructionBody(record NativeRecord) (instructionBody, error) {\n352|\twhere := \"record \" + record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(record.Line)\n353|\tmembers, err := decodeBodyObject(record, []string{\"authority\", \"directives\"}, map[string]bool{\"authority\": true, \"directives\": true})\n354|\tif err != nil {\n355|\t\treturn instructionBody{}, err\n356|\t}\n357|\tauthority, err := bodyString(record, members, \"authority\")\n358|\tif err != nil {\n359|\t\treturn instructionBody{}, err\n360|\t}\n361|\tif authority != \"high\" && authority != \"low\" {\n362|\t\treturn instructionBody{}, invalid(\"%s body authority %q is outside high|low\", where, authority)\n363|\t}\n364|\tvar directives []string\n365|\tif err := json.Unmarshal(members[\"directives\"], &directives); err != nil {\n366|\t\treturn instructionBody{}, invalid(\"%s body member %q is not an array of strings\", where, \"directives\")\n367|\t}\n368|\tif len(directives) > 1024 {\n369|\t\treturn instructionBody{}, invalid(\"%s body carries %d directives, maximum is 1024\", where, len(directives))\n370|\t}\n371|\tfor index, directive := range directives {\n372|\t\tif environ.StringLength(directive) < 1 || environ.StringLength(directive) > 4096 {\n373|\t\t\treturn instructionBody{}, invalid(\"%s body directive[%d] is not a string[1..4096]\", where, index)\n374|\t\t}\n375|\t}\n376|\treturn instructionBody{Authority: authority, Directives: directives}, nil\n377|}\n378|\n379|// toolDefinitionBody is the exact tool-definition body.\n380|type toolDefinitionBody struct {\n381|\tToolName       string\n382|\tDefinitionHash string\n383|\tLiveClaim      bool\n384|}\n385|\n386|// decodeToolDefinitionBody validates the exact definition body. A\n387|// live_attestation claim is parsed so the live-surface gate can\n388|// refuse it: captured history can never self-promote.\n389|func decodeToolDefinitionBody(record NativeRecord) (toolDefinitionBody, error) {\n390|\twhere := \"record \" + record.MemberKey + \" line \" + itoa(record.Line)\n391|\tmembers, err := decodeBodyObject(record,\n392|\t\t[]string{\"tool_name\", \"definition_digest\"},\n393|\t\tmap[string]bool{\"tool_name\": true, \"definition_digest\": true, \"live_attestation\": true})\n394|\tif err != nil {\n395|\t\treturn toolDefinitionBody{}, err\n396|\t}\n397|\tname, err := bodyString(record, members, \"tool_name\")\n398|\tif err != nil {\n399|\t\treturn toolDefinitionBody{}, err\n400|\t}\n401|\tif environ.StringLength(name) < 1 || environ.StringLength(name) > 512 {\n402|\t\treturn toolDefinitionBody{}, invalid(\"%s body tool_name is not a string[1..512]\", where)\n403|\t}\n404|\tdigest, err := bodyString(record, members, \"definition_digest\")\n405|\tif err != nil {\n406|\t\treturn toolDefinitionBody{}, err\n407|\t}\n408|\tlive, err := bodyOptionalBool(record, members, \"live_attestation\")\n409|\tif err != nil {\n410|\t\treturn toolDefinitionBody{}, err\n411|\t}\n412|\treturn toolDefinitionBody{ToolName: name, DefinitionHash: digest, LiveClaim: live}, nil\n413|}\n414|\n415|// toolCallBody is the exact tool-call body.\n416|type toolCallBody struct {\n417|\tCallID   string\n418|\tToolName string\n419|}\n420|\n421|// decodeToolCallBody validates the exact call body.\n422|func 