{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8b7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3cf-5753-7b41-a2b3-ce03595a21fa"},"sequence":694,"recorded_at":1780531400001383,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3d1-4efc-7683-a508-fbff271cf4fe"},"task_id":"01a0b3d1-4efc-7683-a508-fbff271cf4fe","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3d1-4efc-7683-a508-fbff271cf4fe","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree/internal/cloneproject/doc.go`.\n1|package cloneproject\n2|\n3|// This package implements the Section 13.14.1 projection-fidelity\n4|// closure: Normalize derives a Canonical Session and Canonical Events\n5|// from captured bytes (a sealed Clone Capture Manifest, its sealed\n6|// Clone Raw Object Manifest, and the installed payload blobs). It is\n7|// the final leaf of the canonical-session-capture-and-evidence\n8|// story: contracts come from internal/clonebundle, capture from\n9|// internal/clonesnap, and this package owns normalization only.\n10|//\n11|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.7.0, Sections\n12|// 7.8, 10.2, and 13.14.1 (internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md).\n13|//\n14|// The projection input is captured bytes, never hand-written\n15|// Canonical Events: every proof builds a fixture provider store,\n16|// runs clonesnap.Capture over it, and normalizes the sealed output.\n17|// Identical captured bytes produce byte-identical canonical output.\n18|//\n19|// Native records: the provider-native session log this package reads\n20|// is newline-delimited JSON (one record per line) carried by included\n21|// durable capture members. The envelope is fixture-native and NOT a\n22|// specification shape:\n23|//\n24|//\t{\"v\":1,\"native_event_id\":\"...\",\"native_type\":\"...\",\n25|//\t \"origin\":\"native|foreign\",\"protection\":\"none|encrypted|signed\",\n26|//\t \"actor\":\"main|subagent:<name>|external\",\"body\":{...}}\n27|//\n28|// Projection rules (each driven and mutated, see TRACEABILITY.md):\n29|//\n30|//   - Unknown native types become raw-addressable opaque_event\n31|//     records with opaque visibility, a whole-record byte-range\n32|//     reference, and reason unknown_native_event. Unknown-class\n33|//     members become one whole-member opaque_event. Nothing\n34|//     attributable is dropped, guessed, or re-typed.\n35|//   - Foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes opaque_reasoning\n36|//     with opaque visibility, preserved byte-exact through the blob\n37|//     store, never decrypted, re-encoded, summarized, truncated, or\n38|//     promoted. Foreign instructions are low-authority history: they\n39|//     never change the effective instruction snapshot.\n40|//   - Historical tools are inert. A tool_definition_snapshot never\n41|//     registers a callable tool (a captured live claim refuses).\n42|//     A tool_call resolves completed only with its tool_result;\n43|//     otherwise it becomes aborted history with reason\n44|//     unsafe_pending_action. Pending actions require a live work\n45|//     order, which capture never carries, so the live surface is\n46|//     always empty.\n47|//   - Source usage is counted into the source ledger only; target\n48|//     accounting stays zero.\n49|//   - Message-like text over 64 KiB becomes a Blob Descriptor\n50|//     reference to an installed overflow blob, never a truncation.\n51|//\n52|// Reuse, not fork: manifests, sessions, events, evidence, and the\n53|// unstable/maximal-safe gates come from internal/clonebundle;\n54|// overflow Blob Descriptors seal through clonesnap.BuildBlobDescriptor\n55|// and install through clonebundle.InstallRawBlob onto the landed\n56|// localstore no-replace discipline; digests, UUIDv7, and character\n57|// measures come from internal/scalar and internal/environ. No rule\n58|// is reimplemented where a landed owner exists.\n59|//\n60|// Stated bounds (not waived): the fixture-native record envelope is\n61|// test-defined, not a specification shape; per-kind payload fact\n62|// registries cover exactly the facts this package emits for the nine\n63|// fixture-native known types (other Canonical kinds are never\n64|// emitted here); framing-malformed lines (unparseable JSON, missing\n65|// envelope members, contradictory protection claims, unknown body\n66|// members) refuse instead of projecting; turn IDs and source\n67|// timestamps are always null; tool call arguments are not carried;\n68|// unknown-class excluded members project nothing (their bytes were\n69|// never captured); 13.14.2-13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions,\n70|// projection planning, transaction, lineage) are sibling scope.","final_result":true}}}
