{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8c3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3cf-5753-7b41-a2b3-ce03595a21fa"},"sequence":700,"recorded_at":1780531400001395,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3d146d671c280891404f058ed72","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree/internal/cloneproject/doc.go`.\n1|package cloneproject\n2|\n3|// This package implements the Section 13.14.1 projection-fidelity\n4|// closure: Normalize derives a Canonical Session and Canonical Events\n5|// from captured bytes (a sealed Clone Capture Manifest, its sealed\n6|// Clone Raw Object Manifest, and the installed payload blobs). It is\n7|// the final leaf of the canonical-session-capture-and-evidence\n8|// story: contracts come from internal/clonebundle, capture from\n9|// internal/clonesnap, and this package owns normalization only.\n10|//\n11|// Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.7.0, Sections\n12|// 7.8, 10.2, and 13.14.1 (internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md).\n13|//\n14|// The projection input is captured bytes, never hand-written\n15|// Canonical Events: every proof builds a fixture provider store,\n16|// runs clonesnap.Capture over it, and normalizes the sealed output.\n17|// Identical captured bytes produce byte-identical canonical output.\n18|//\n19|// Native records: the provider-native session log this package reads\n20|// is newline-delimited JSON (one record per line) carried by included\n21|// durable capture members. The envelope is fixture-native and NOT a\n22|// specification shape:\n23|//\n24|//\t{\"v\":1,\"native_event_id\":\"...\",\"native_type\":\"...\",\n25|//\t \"origin\":\"native|foreign\",\"protection\":\"none|encrypted|signed\",\n26|//\t \"actor\":\"main|subagent:<name>|external\",\"body\":{...}}\n27|//\n28|// Projection rules (each driven and mutated, see TRACEABILITY.md):\n29|//\n30|//   - Unknown native types become raw-addressable opaque_event\n31|//     records with opaque visibility, a whole-record byte-range\n32|//     reference, and reason unknown_native_event. Unknown-class\n33|//     members become one whole-member opaque_event. Nothing\n34|//     attributable is dropped, guessed, or re-typed.\n35|//   - Foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes opaque_reasoning\n36|//     with opaque visibility, preserved byte-exact through the blob\n37|//     store, never decrypted, re-encoded, summarized, truncated, or\n38|//     promoted. Foreign instructions are low-authority history: they\n39|//     never change the effective instruction snapshot.\n40|//   - Historical tools are inert. A tool_definition_snapshot never\n41|//     registers a callable tool (a captured live claim refuses).\n42|//     A tool_call resolves completed only with its tool_result;\n43|//     otherwise it becomes aborted history with reason\n44|//     unsafe_pending_action. Pending actions require a live work\n45|//     order, which capture never carries, so the live surface is\n46|//     always empty.\n47|//   - Source usage is counted into the source ledger only; target\n48|//     accounting stays zero.\n49|//   - Message-like text over 64 KiB becomes a Blob Descriptor\n50|//     reference to an installed overflow blob, never a truncation.\n51|//\n52|// Reuse, not fork: manifests, sessions, events, evidence, and the\n53|// unstable/maximal-safe gates come from internal/clonebundle;\n54|// overflow Blob Descriptors seal through clonesnap.BuildBlobDescriptor\n55|// and install through clonebundle.InstallRawBlob onto the landed\n56|// localstore no-replace discipline; digests, UUIDv7, and character\n57|// measures come from internal/scalar and internal/environ. No rule\n58|// is reimplemented where a landed owner exists.\n59|//\n60|// Stated bounds (not waived): the fixture-native record envelope is\n61|// test-defined, not a specification shape; per-kind payload fact\n62|// registries cover exactly the facts this package emits for the nine\n63|// fixture-native known types (other Canonical kinds are never\n64|// emitted here); framing-malformed lines (unparseable JSON, missing\n65|// envelope members, contradictory protection claims, unknown body\n66|// members) refuse instead of projecting; turn IDs and source\n67|// timestamps are always null; tool call arguments are not carried;\n68|// unknown-class excluded members project nothing (their bytes were\n69|// never captured); 13.14.2-13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions,\n70|// projection planning, transaction, lineage) are sibling scope.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8c5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3cf-5753-7b41-a2b3-ce03595a21fa"},"sequence":701,"recorded_at":1780531400001397,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3d149217663ad9f0e8f1d9357a8","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree/internal/cloneproject/overflow.go`.\n1|package cloneproject\n2|\n3|// This file carries the 64 KiB message-like content rule: inline\n4|// text at or under the bound seals inline; anything larger becomes a\n5|// Blob Descriptor reference to an installed overflow blob. Oversized\n6|// content is never truncated, summarized, or refused: the bytes move\n7|// to the blob store and the reference resolves back to them exactly.\n8|\n9|import (\n10|\t\"bytes\"\n11|\n12|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/clonebundle\"\n13|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/clonesnap\"\n14|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/localstore\"\n15|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n16|)\n17|\n18|// maxInlineContentBytes is the Section 13.14.1 inline content bound:\n19|// inline content is at most 64 KiB, measured in bytes exactly as the\n20|// landed content-block gate measures it.\n21|const maxInlineContentBytes = 65536\n22|\n23|// overflowMediaType labels overflow text blobs.\n24|const overflowMediaType = \"text/plain\"\n25|\n26|// OverflowBlob is one installed overflow blob with its verified\n27|// identities.\n28|type OverflowBlob struct {\n29|\t// BlobID is the SHA-256 of the content bytes.\n30|\tBlobID scalar.Digest\n31|\t// DescriptorID is the omit-self identity of the descriptor the\n32|\t// content block references.\n33|\tDescriptorID scalar.Digest\n34|\t// Size is the content length.\n35|\tSize uint64\n36|}\n37|\n38|// installOverflow installs oversized text through the landed\n39|// discipline: the descriptor seals through\n40|// clonesnap.BuildBlobDescriptor, the payload installs through\n41|// clonebundle.InstallRawBlob (identity plus blob-ID/size agreement),\n42|// and the descriptor bytes install under their content digest so the\n43|// reference resolves. Both installs are content-addressed and\n44|// idempotent: a replay verifies and reuses.\n45|func installOverflow(sink *localstore.ObjectStore, text string) (OverflowBlob, error) {\n46|\tpayload := []byte(text)\n47|\tdescriptor, err := clonesnap.BuildBlobDescriptor(payload)\n48|\tif err != nil {\n49|\t\treturn OverflowBlob{}, invalid(\"content overflow cannot seal its blob descriptor: %v\", err)\n50|\t}\n51|\tif _, err := clonebundle.InstallRawBlob(sink, descriptor.Descriptor, bytes.NewReader(payload)); err != nil {\n52|\t\treturn OverflowBlob{}, invalid(\"content overflow cannot install its payload: %v\", err)\n53|\t}\n54|\tcontentID := scalar.SHA256Digest(descriptor.Descriptor)\n55|\tif _, err := sink.PutBlob(contentID, uint64(len(descriptor.Descriptor)), bytes.NewReader(descriptor.Descriptor)); err != nil {\n56|\t\treturn OverflowBlob{}, invalid(\"content overflow cannot install its descriptor: %v\", err)\n57|\t}\n58|\treturn OverflowBlob{BlobID: descriptor.BlobID, DescriptorID: descriptor.DescriptorID, Size: descriptor.Size}, nil\n59|}\n60|\n61|// contentBlockForText builds one text content block: inline content\n62|// at or under 64 KiB, a Blob Descriptor reference above it.\n63|func contentBlockForText(text string, sink *localstore.ObjectStore) (map[string]any, []OverflowBlob, error) {\n64|\tif len(text) > maxInlineContentBytes {\n65|\t\tinstalled, err := installOverflow(sink, text)\n66|\t\tif err != nil {\n67|\t\t\treturn nil, nil, err\n68|\t\t}\n69|\t\treturn map[string]any{\n70|\t\t\t\"type\":               \"text\",\n71|\t\t\t\"blob_descriptor_id\": installed.DescriptorID.String(),\n72|\t\t\t\"media_type\":         overflowMediaType,\n73|\t\t}, []OverflowBlob{installed}, nil\n74|\t}\n75|\treturn map[string]any{\n76|\t\t\"type\":    \"text\",\n77|\t\t\"content\": text,\n78|\t}, nil, nil\n79|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8c7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3cf-5753-7b41-a2b3-ce03595a21fa"},"sequence":702,"recorded_at":1780531400001399,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3d14b85771da15bef68b4cb3569","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree/internal/cloneproject/errors.go`.\n1|package cloneproject\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"errors\"\n5|\t\"fmt\"\n6|)\n7|\n8|// ErrInvalid is the refusal for every malformed projection input and\n9|// every fidelity violation: undecodable manifests, unstable or\n10|// mismatched capture closure, missing or disagreeing blobs,\n11|// malformed native framing, contradictory protection claims, live\n12|// authority claimed by captured history, and ambiguous tool\n13|// pairings. Callers match with errors.Is; the message names the\n14|// offending member, record, or blob.\n15|var ErrInvalid = errors.New(\"cloneproject: invalid projection\")\n16|\n17|func invalid(format string, arguments ...any) error {\n18|\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %s\", ErrInvalid, fmt.Sprintf(format, arguments...))\n19|}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
