{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8f1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3cf-5753-7b41-a2b3-ce03595a21fa"},"sequence":723,"recorded_at":1780531400001441,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c"},"call_id":"call_01a0b3d155ae73939d196c0d185bfc20","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree/internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n1|# Projection Fidelity Clause Coverage (TASK-260830-32ypr2)\n2|\n3|Owner: `internal/cloneproject`. Authority:\n4|`internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.7.0.md`, Sections 7.8, 10.2, 13.14.1\n5|(the pinned sections are byte-identical to v0.6.0).\n6|This is the FINAL leaf's clause record for the projection-fidelity\n7|closure; the `internal/traceability` registry bindings and re-pin\n8|ship in this leaf as well (see the Story-close section below).\n9|\n10|## Why this package normalizes instead of clonebundle or clonesnap\n11|\n12|The first leaf (`internal/clonebundle`) owns the capture contracts:\n13|the closed manifest/boundary/session/event shapes, their builders\n14|and decoders. The second leaf (`internal/clonesnap`) owns the\n15|capture OPERATION over a real provider store. This package owns\n16|NORMALIZATION: deriving Canonical Sessions and Canonical Events\n17|from captured bytes. Every event and the session seal through the\n18|landed `clonebundle` builders (`BuildCanonicalEvent`,\n19|`BuildCanonicalSession`, `CheckOrdinalContiguity`,\n20|`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `InstallRawBlob`) and re-decode through\n21|the landed decoders before return; overflow Blob Descriptors seal\n22|through `clonesnap.BuildBlobDescriptor`; no second manifest,\n23|session, event, blob, or identity model exists here.\n24|\n25|## Landed-owner reuse\n26|\n27|| Scope | Owner | Use |\n28||---|---|---|\n29|| Session/event/evidence shapes | `internal/clonebundle` | all Build/Decode/Check/Refuse entries above |\n30|| Overflow descriptor shape | `internal/clonesnap` | `BuildBlobDescriptor` (errors wrapped with the overflow cause) |\n31|| Blob install (no-replace, fsync, verify) | `internal/clonebundle` + `internal/localstore` | `InstallRawBlob`, `ObjectStore.PutBlob` |\n32|| Digests, UUIDv7, timestamps | `internal/scalar` | `ParseDigest`, `SHA256Digest`, `ParseUUIDv7` |\n33|| Character string measure | `internal/environ` | `StringLength` at every native bound |\n34|| Canonical bytes | `internal/canonicaljson` | `Canonicalize`, `CalculateObjectIdentity` (tests resolve overflow descriptors) |\n35|\n36|## Fixture-native per-kind payload fact registry\n37|\n38|Section 13.14.1 requires payloads to carry only their registered\n39|typed facts. The envelope and value model are landed (`checkPayload`\n40|in `clonebundle`); this package registers the exact facts it emits\n41|for each kind it projects. No other Canonical kind is emitted here.\n42|\n43|| Kind | Exact facts |\n44||---|---|\n45|| `user_message`, `assistant_message`, `reasoning_summary` | `content_blocks` (one `text` block, inline at or under 64 KiB, else `blob_descriptor_id` + `media_type`), `extensions` |\n46|| `opaque_reasoning` | `protection` (`encrypted`\\|`signed`), `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n47|| `opaque_event` (unknown record) | `native_type`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n48|| `opaque_event` (protected known record) | `native_type`, `protection`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n49|| `opaque_event` (unknown member) | `native_item_key`, `byte_count`, `blob_descriptor_id`, `extensions` |\n50|| `instruction_snapshot` | `authority` (`low` forced for foreign), `directives`, `extensions` |\n51|| `tool_definition_snapshot` | `tool_name`, `definition_digest`, `callable` (always false), `extensions` |\n52|| `tool_call` | `call_id`, `tool_name`, `resolution` (`completed`\\|`aborted`), `extensions` |\n53|| `tool_result` | `call_id`, `status` (`ok`\\|`error`), `resolution`, `extensions` |\n54|| `usage` | `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `extensions` |\n55|\n56|## Clause map\n57|\n58|| Pinned clause | Production entry | Test |\n59||---|---|---|\n60|| 13.14.1 unknown native records become raw-addressable opaque events | `Normalize`, `dispatchRecord` | `TestNormalizeUnknownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` (kind, `opaque` visibility, `unknown_native_event` reason, raw range resolves to the exact line) |\n61|| 13.14.1 almost-known records are never coerced into a neighbouring kind | `dispatchRecord` (exact type switch) | `TestNormalizeAlmostKnownRecordBecomesOpaqueEvent` (`message/smoke` stays `opaque_event`, never `user_message`) |\n62|| 13.14.1 unknown-class members become whole-member opaque events | `collectMembers` | `TestNormalizeUnknownMemberBecomesWholeMemberOpaque` (offset 0, full length, null native IDs, resolves to the whole member) |\n63|| 13.14.1 opaque events are never dropped, guessed, or re-typed | `Normalize` (deterministic order) | `TestNormalizeOpaqueIsStableAcrossProjections` (project twice, byte-identical, still `opaque_event`) |\n64|| 13.14.1 foreign encrypted reasoning is opaque-preserved | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeForeignEncryptedReasoningStaysOpaque` (`opaque_reasoning`, `foreign_encrypted_payload`, no content members, byte-exact round trip) |\n65|| 13.14.1 foreign signed reasoning is opaque-preserved | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeForeignSignedReasoningStaysOpaque` (`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, byte-exact) |\n66|| 13.14.1 native protected reasoning stays opaque with no foreign code | `dispatchProtected`, `cryptoReasons` | `TestNormalizeNativeProtectedReasoningStaysOpaque` (empty reasons) |\n67|| 13.14.1 protected known content never reaches a semantic kind | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeProtectedMessageBecomesOpaqueEvent` (encrypted assistant message is `opaque_event`) |\n68|| 13.14.1 unknown+protected records carry both stable reasons | `dispatchProtected` | `TestNormalizeUnknownProtectedRecordCarriesBothReasons` |\n69|| 13.14.1 foreign instructions are low-authority history | `dispatchInstruction`, `foldInstructions` | `TestNormalizeForeignInstructionCannotChangeEffectiveSnapshot` (effective snapshot native-only, foreign payload pins `low`), `TestNormalizeForeignOnlyInstructionLeavesSnapshotEmpty` |\n70|| 13.14.1 source usage is not target accounting | `foldUsage` | `TestNormalizeSourceUsageIsNotTargetAccounting` (source sums exact, target zero) |\n71|| 13.14.1 historical tools are inert; call+result resolves completed | `resolveToolCalls`, `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_with_result` (kinds, `internal` visibility, `completed`, empty live surface) |\n72|| 13.14.1 incomplete calls become aborted history and block pending action | `resolveToolCalls`, `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/call_without_result` (`aborted`, `unsafe_pending_action`, empty live surface), `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/result_without_call` (orphan `aborted`) |\n73|| 13.14.1 results arriving after the boundary complete the same call | `resolveToolCalls` over two captures | `TestNormalizeResultAfterBoundaryCompletes` (first capture `aborted`, second `completed`) |\n74|| 13.14.1 nested calls attribute to a parented subagent actor | `checkActors`, `buildResult` | `TestNormalizeToolMatrix/nested_subagent_call` (subagent actor, parent is main) |\n75|| 13.14.1 definitions never register a callable tool | `deriveLiveSurface`, `dispatchDefinition` | `TestNormalizeToolDefinitionNeverRegistersCallable` (`callable` false, `CallableTools` empty) |\n76|| 13.14.1 live surface stays empty over mixed history | `deriveLiveSurface` | `TestNormalizeLiveSurfaceStaysEmpty` |\n77|| 13.14.1 Canonical Session bounds (actors, ordered event IDs, head) | `buildResult` | `TestNormalizeSealsSessionShape` (ordinals, parent chain, head is last) |\n78|| 13.14.1 message-like inline content at most 64 KiB; oversized becomes a blob reference | `contentBlockForText`, `installOverflow` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (65536 inline, 65537 blob-referenced and byte-exact, never truncated) |\n79|| 13.14.1 same captured bytes project byte-identical output | `Normalize` (sorted inputs, no clock) | `TestNormalizeIsDeterministic` |\n80|| 13.14.1 unstable_archive cannot enter target projection | `Normalize` via `RefuseUnstableForTarget` | `TestNormalizeRefusesUnstableCapture` |\n81|| 13.14.1 capture closure: manifest link, blob fetch, digest/size agreement | `Normalize`, `collectMembers` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/manifest_closure_drift/tampered_blob/missing_blob` |\n82|| 13.14.1 framing-malformed records refuse with member+line named | `splitRecordLines`, `parseNativeLine`, body decoders | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/malformed_json_line/missing_envelope_member/bad_envelope_version/blank_line/unknown_body_member/contradictory_protection/protected_plaintext_body/invalid_utf8_line` |\n83|| 13.14.1 live claims by captured history refuse | `deriveLiveSurface`, `resolveToolCalls` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/live_attestation_claim/live_followup_claim` |\n84|| 13.14.1 ambiguous tool pairings refuse | `resolveToolCalls` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/duplicate_call_id/duplicate_result_id` |\n85|| 13.14.1 exact actor mapping (referenced iff mapped) | `checkActors` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/unmapped_actor/unmapped_extra_actor/main_actor_in_map` |\n86|| 13.14.1 instruction authority and usage value model | `decodeInstructionBody`, `bodyUint53` | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/bad_instruction_authority/fractional_usage/unsafe_usage_magnitude` |\n87|| 10.2 Blob Descriptor reference resolves to installed bytes | `installOverflow` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (`mustResolveOverflow` through the sink) |\n88|| 10.2 fsync + verify + atomic install before referencing | `InstallRawBlob`, `PutBlob` (landed) | `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` (replay verifies and reuses, blob count stable) |\n89|| 7.8 large data by reference, never embedded | `contentBlockForText` | `TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary` (65537-byte text is a reference, not an embedded frame) |\n90|| 1.6 string measure in characters | `environ.StringLength` at every native bound | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable` bound rows (call/actor/directive widths refuse past the character bound) |\n91|| 1.6 text is valid UTF-8, never rewritten | line-level `utf8.Valid` before decode | `TestNormalizeRefusalTable/invalid_utf8_line` |\n92|\n93|## Durability\n94|\n95|This package holds no local state. Its only durable write is\n96|overflow-blob installation: payload bytes through the landed\n97|`InstallRawBlob` (descriptor identity plus blob-ID/size agreement)\n98|and descriptor bytes through `ObjectStore.PutBlob`, both\n99|content-addressed under the landed no-replace discipline (stage,\n100|fsync, verify, atomic install). Crash semantics are the landed\n101|`localstore` discipline's (proven by that package's fault suites);\n102|this package adds bundle atomicity at the return:\n103|`TestNormalizeFailureReturnsNoPartialBundle` proves a mid-projection\n104|fetch failure returns no partial bundle and a healthy re-run\n105|converges, and `TestNormalizeIsIdempotentIntoSharedSink` proves a\n106|replay into a shared sink seals byte-identical output while the sink\n107|blob count stays stable (verify-and-reuse, no reinstall). A refused\n108|projection may leave orphan overflow blobs from earlier units in the\n109|sink; they are content-addressed and inert, and no bundle ever\n110|references them.\n111|\n112|## Mutants\n113|\n114|`testdata/mutant_harness.py` ships 49 narrowing rows plus the\n115|harmless `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED control. Every row weakens one\n116|gate to admit exactly one member of the class it must reject, and\n117|every killer drives the production `Normalize` entry over real\n118|captured bytes. `N-native-type-token` and `N-protection-encrypted`\n119|are the token-preserving attacks: the searched-for text still\n120|matches while the decision changes, and the killers execute the\n121|behavioral suite. No row is an arm-delete; no plant covers two\n122|sites. The battery runs twice with one raw log per plant per run\n123|carrying the subprocess exit.\n124|\n125|## Stated bounds (sibling scope, not waived)\n126|\n127|- The fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing, not a\n128|  specification shape: `v`, `native_event_id`, `native_type`,\n129|  `origin`, `protection`, `actor`, `body`. Real providers define\n130|  their own native logs; the adapter layer is `sessadapter` scope.\n131|- Per-kind payload facts cover exactly the registry above. Other\n132|  Canonical kinds (`session_started`, `approval_request`,\n133|  `plan_update`, `progress`, `rate_limit`, `file_change`,\n134|  `compaction`, `turn_*`, `subagent_*`, `error`,\n135|  `migration_checkpoint`, `session_finished`) are never emitted\n136|  here; their fact registries are normalization-sibling scope.\n137|- Framing-malformed lines refuse (unparseable JSON, missing\n138|  envelope members, blank lines, invalid UTF-8, contradictory\n139|  protection claims, unknown body members inside a known type)\n140|  instead of projecting: without attributable identity a line\n141|  cannot become evidence. Type-level unknowns become\n142|  `opaque_event`.\n143|- Native-protected records carry no reason code: the closed core\n144|  reasons name foreign causes only, and extension reasons are\n145|  operator scope. The payload `protection` fact carries the cause.\n146|- Turn IDs and source timestamps are always null: turns are not\n147|  reconstructed and source clocks are not trusted.\n148|- Tool call arguments are not carried: calls are inert history\n149|  identified by call ID and tool name.\n150|- Unknown-class excluded members project nothing: their bytes were\n151|  never captured.\n152|- Sections 13.14.2-13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, projection\n153|  planning, Migration Checkpoint, lineage, transaction, tuple\n154|  admission) are sibling scope: this story plans no projection,\n155|  stages no target, and admits no tuple.\n156|- Section 7.8 operation wiring (capture-plan/capture/normalize\n157|  frames) stays owned by `sessadapter`; this package owns the\n158|  fidelity rules those operations must satisfy, not the frames.\n159|- The `pending` live-work-order map parameter of\n160|  `deriveLiveSurface` is live-sibling API: `Normalize` always\n161|  passes nil, so nothing captured can pend.\n162|\n163|## Story-close (FINAL leaf)\n164|\n165|This leaf binds the story's normative sections in\n166|`internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json`:\n167|\n168|- `section:7.8` is bound FULL (2/2): clause `7.8#1` (large data by\n169|  reference) discharges through the new `clone-projection-fidelity`\n170|  acceptance case (`TestNormalizeInlineContentBoundary`); clause\n171|  `7.8#2` (execution bindings equal freshly read facts) discharges\n172|  through the new `session-adapter-call-binding` case\n173|  (`TestCheckCallBinding` plus the zero-facts refusal test, both\n174|  committed by the sessadapter owner).\n175|- `section:10.2` is bound FULL (5/5): `10.2#1` through\n176|  `clone-capture-contracts`, `10.2#3`–`10.2#5` through\n177|  `clone-native-capture`, and `10.2#2` through both\n178|  `clone-native-capture` (capture install) and\n179|  `clone-projection-fidelity` (overflow install and idempotent\n180|  replay).\n181|- `section:13.14.1` carries no RFC 2119 keyword line the\n182|  `tracecheck` scanner can see (its obligations are closed-shape\n183|  \"contains exactly\" sentences), so no registry binding can\n184|  enumerate it: it would measure `unmeasured`, which assigned-scope\n185|  admission deliberately refuses. The story's 13.14.1 clause record\n186|  is therefore the three package `TRACEABILITY.md` files plus the\n187|  three leaf conformance matrices, executed by the three real\n188|  suites bound as `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`,\n189|  and `clone-projection-fidelity`.\n190|- `reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256` in\n191|  `internal/traceability/traceability.go` is re-derived from the\n192|  edited registry (derivation command and output in\n193|  `TASK-260830-32ypr2_results.md`).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
