{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c9bb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3cf-5753-7b41-a2b3-ce03595a21fa"},"sequence":824,"recorded_at":1780531400001643,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3d1-988d-7930-9dab-1f8f2d88951b"},"task_id":"01a0b3d1-988d-7930-9dab-1f8f2d88951b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3d1-988d-7930-9dab-1f8f2d88951b","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev1/pred-verdict.md`.\n(91 line(s) above)\n92|### P3 — sub-members, axes and sibling arms with no committed row (production correct in every case; each plant SURVIVED the whole suite 2/2 and its admitted behaviour was executed under the plant, `logs/under-mutant/*.log`)\n93|\n94|- **P3-a Row 8 digest LABELLING is pinned against the pipeline's own claim.**\n95|  `R3-archive-swaps-pre-post` (the unstable form seals the post-capture\n96|  measurement as `pre_capture_digest` and vice versa, and `CaptureResult`\n97|  reports the same swap) **SURVIVED 2/2**. The rev3 assertion compares the\n98|  sealed digests to `result.PreDigest`/`PostDigest` — the pipeline's own\n99|  values (shape (a) of the producer brief: an expectation derived from\n100|  production). Under the plant (probe PA): `sealed_pre == quiet_d0 = false`,\n101|  `sealed_post == quiet_d0 = true`, `sealed_pre == result_pre = true` — the\n102|  committed test passes while the archive manifest labels the digests\n103|  backwards. Pristine: `sealed_pre == quiet_d0 = true`. The independent\n104|  oracle is cheap and already in the suite's vocabulary: a quiet `Capture`\n105|  over an identical unmutated fixture seals `pre == post == D0`; assert the\n106|  archive's `pre_capture_digest == D0` and `post_capture_digest != D0`. Ship\n107|  a harness row of the `R3-archive-swaps-pre-post` shape.\n108|- **P3-b RaceArchive over a QUIET source is unmeasured (rule pinned along one\n109|  axis).** `R3-archive-policy-always-unstable` (under `RaceArchive` +\n110|  `OperatorExplicit` every capture seals `unstable_archive` before the gate\n111|  runs) **SURVIVED 2/2**. Every committed archive-policy row injects a\n112|  mutation; none drives the policy over an unmutated store. Under the plant\n113|  (probe PB) a quiet store seals `kind=unstable_archive` carrying\n114|  `source_not_quiescent` with `pre == post`, and target admission refuses it;\n115|  pristine seals `stable` and admits. One row: `OnRace=RaceArchive`,\n116|  `OperatorExplicit=true`, no hook → `BoundaryKind == \"stable\"`,\n117|  `AdmitForTarget` admits.\n118|- **P3-c A failure to re-list the store at POST time is unpinned (absence vs\n119|  failure to read).** `R3-post-enumerate-failure-as-quiet` (`measurePost`\n120|  treats an enumeration error as \"no change\") **SURVIVED 2/2**. Under it\n121|  (probe PD, `store/` chmod 000 in `AfterWalk`) the capture **seals `stable`,\n122|  `raw_complete=true`, and publishes both manifests**; pristine refuses\n123|  `capture cannot enumerate store member \"store\": … permission denied` with\n124|  nothing published. The committed \"unreadable at post\" row\n125|  (`TestCaptureRaceUnreadableAtPost`) reaches the MEMBER-unreadable arm\n126|  (`openMember` fails → unknown content → digests differ), not the\n127|  enumeration arm (`walk.go:85` via `measurePost`, never executed by the\n128|  suite — `logs/refusal-site-census.txt`). One row (skip when euid 0):\n129|  chmod 000 the `store/` directory in `AfterWalk`, restore in `t.Cleanup`,\n130|  assert the refusal names `\"store\"` and the capture store holds no manifest.\n131|- **P3-d A subdirectory that cannot be listed at WALK time is unpinned.**\n132|  `R3-enumerate-unreadable-as-empty` (an unreadable subdirectory enumerates\n133|  as empty) **SURVIVED 2/2**. Under it (probe PE) a planned optional member\n134|  inside a chmod-000 directory seals as `plan_optional_absent` and the\n135|  manifest carries `raw_complete=true` — a completeness claim laundered from\n136|  a read failure; pristine refuses `capture cannot enumerate store member\n137|  \"locked\"` with zero blobs. The `walk.go` doc comment \"A failed observation\n138|  is a refusal, never an absence\" is prose that outruns the tests (shape (f)).\n139|  One row, or restate as a bound.\n140|- **P3-e The race window is measurable only through the `AfterWalk` seam —\n141|  state the bound.** `R3-post-measure-only-with-hook` (`measurePost` runs only\n142|  when `Hooks.AfterWalk != nil`; every hook-less capture reports `post ==\n143|  pre` without re-reading) **SURVIVED 2/2**. No deterministic seam-free\n144|  injection exists (a concurrent mutator cannot be ordered against the\n145|  pipeline without a hook), so this is a bound to STATE in TRACEABILITY and\n146|  the results (\"the mutation window is exercised only through the AfterWalk\n147|  seam; `measurePost` is unconditional by inspection\"), not a row to add. It\n148|  is not stated today.\n149|- **P3-f Exported `BuildAdmissionReceipt` standalone profile gate unpinned\n150|  (the P3-η shape at this leaf).** `R3-receipt-profile-unchecked` (the\n151|  standalone entry admits exactly profile `ultra`) **SURVIVED 2/2**; under it\n152|  (probe PF) `BuildAdmissionReceipt(…, \"ultra\")` seals a receipt carrying\n153|  `\"fidelity_profile\":\"ultra\"`; pristine refuses. The composed path is pinned\n154|  (`AdmitForTarget` refuses first, `N-fidelity` KILLED), but the exported\n155|  entry advertises its own check that no test drives (`project.go:181` never\n156|  executed). One direct call, or state the bound.\n157|- **P3-g Two smaller unrowed refusal sub-classes.** (i) `R3-empty-cwd-as-root`\n158|  (an EMPTY workspace cwd seals as `\".\"`) **SURVIVED 2/2** — probe PH: the\n159|  binding seals `cwd_relative:\".\"` for an unobserved cwd; pristine refuses\n160|  `cwd_relative is empty` (`workspace.go:113`, never executed). (ii)\n161|  `R3-drop-early-containment-pass` (ARM-DELETE, labelled) **SURVIVED 2/2** —\n162|  the early containment pass's doc claim \"this pass fails fast with nothing\n163|  installed\" is unpinned: probe PG plants a planned FIFO that sorts AFTER an\n164|  included member; pristine installs 0 blobs before refusing, the plant\n165|  installs 1. Either assert zero blobs in a row with that ordering or reword\n166|  the comment (orphan payload blobs on seal-time refusals are already a\n167|  recorded informational).\n168|\n169|### Informational (no action required unless cheap)\n170|\n171|- `R3-early-pass-opens-excluded-special` (ARM-DELETE, OVER-STRICT direction)\n172|  SURVIVED 2/2: an excluded-class special member (symlink credential) is the\n173|  only shape where \"excluded members are never opened\" is measured by nothing\n174|  but the rev2 probe P13a and my probe PI (pristine: `kind=stable`, no leak,\n175|  never opened; under the plant the Guard refuses it — safe direction).\n176|- `R3-nil-target-sink-unchecked` (ARM-DELETE) SURVIVED 2/2: a nil target sink\n177|  refuses before any capture on pristine (probe PJ, capture store empty);\n178|  under the plant the capture publishes both manifests and then fails at the\n179|  receipt with the landed \"object store is not initialized\" (no panic). rev2\n180|  informational, unchanged.\n181|- The four `N-exclude-*` narrowings are killed by the landed raw-manifest\n182|  builder (\"raw object entry[0] class \"credential\" is outside the raw\n183|  subset\"), i.e. at seal time after the excluded bytes were already opened\n184|  and installed as an orphan payload blob; the leak class itself is pinned\n185|  by the add-write `N-excluded-orphan-blob` (blob scan). Attribution only.\n186|  `clonesnap.excludedClass` spells the four-class table that the landed\n187|  `clonebundle.alwaysExcludedClass` (unexported) also spells — the same\n188|  \"spelled twice\" shape the producer already records for the fidelity\n189|  vocabulary (P3-ζ′); worth listing beside it.\n190|- An unknown fidelity profile is refused only AFTER the capture has sealed\n191|  and published both manifests (`CaptureAndProject` → `sealAndPublish` →\n192|  `admitAndEmit` → `AdmitForTarget`); the manifests are valid and\n193|  content-addressed, so nothing is wrong, but an entry-time\n194|  `validFidelityProfile` check would avoid the durable writes.\n195|- Refusal-site census (`logs/refusal-site-census.txt`, coverprofile over the\n196|  committed suite): 25 of 60 `invalid(` call sites are executed; of the 35\n197|  unexecuted, 26 are defensive or unreachable by construction (serialize /\n198|  canonicalize / re-decode of builder-sealed bytes, `PutBlob` faults on a\n199|  healthy store, negative sizes, read-vs-stat TOCTOU windows, the in-memory\n200|  128 GiB descriptor bound behind the `openMember` limit, the\n201|  \"archive unexpectedly admitted\" arm behind `AdmitForTarget`) and 9 are\n202|  reachable classes with no committed row: `walk.go:85` (P3-c/d),\n203|  `walk.go:90` (backslash-named member; the plan gate refuses it anyway),\n204|  `capture.go:208` (relative store root: `OpenNoFollowDir` admits a relative\n205|  path that exists, `NewGuard` refuses it — rev2 probe P5), `capture.go:460`\n206|  (`AfterRawPublish` hook returning an error; `TestCaptureRefusesHookError`\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
