{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ce57","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3cf-5753-7b41-a2b3-ce03595a21fa"},"sequence":1414,"recorded_at":1780531400002823,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.started","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3d7-7300-7343-913a-de0c4a64dc62"},"task_id":"01a0b3d7-7300-7343-913a-de0c4a64dc62","event":{"kind":"started","task_id":"01a0b3d7-7300-7343-913a-de0c4a64dc62","span_id":"b2cbe103f01a1a7b"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ce59","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3cf-5753-7b41-a2b3-ce03595a21fa"},"sequence":1415,"recorded_at":1780531400002825,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3d7-7300-7343-913a-de0c4a64dc62"},"task_id":"01a0b3d7-7300-7343-913a-de0c4a64dc62","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3d7-7300-7343-913a-de0c4a64dc62","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree/README.md`.\n(3137 line(s) above)\n3138|## Specification-to-Code Ownership Gate\n3139|\n3140|[`internal/traceability`](internal/traceability) provides the read-only\n3141|repository gate used by CI. Its reviewed\n3142|[`ownership.v0.7.0.json`](internal/traceability/ownership.v0.7.0.json)\n3143|registry independently enumerates implementation owners for all 64 current\n3144|contract rows, 36 pinned or catalog-referenced normative section keys, 144\n3145|executable acceptance cases, 68 exact section bindings with their declared\n3146|coverage, 7 disclosed unowned sections, and 33 exact fixture identities or\n3147|Appendix D anchors. The v0.4.3 projection is checked as an owned 55-contract subset,\n3148|and the superseded v0.6.0 and v0.5.0 registries are checked as owned legacy projections.\n3149|The generated v0.7.0 catalog also carries the reviewed schema/version/self-field\n3150|contracts used by canonical object identity calculation; generator validation\n3151|binds each row to a pinned contract and rejects duplicate, unsupported,\n3152|malformed, or digest-drifted metadata.\n3153|\n3154|The production validator re-verifies the exact source lock and reviewed catalog\n3155|metadata, refuses stale generated output, requires every production and test\n3156|owner to resolve to a real Go declaration, and rejects gaps, duplicates,\n3157|self-minted keys, partial or malformed reads, and semantic ownership drift.\n3158|GitHub Actions invokes the gate directly before generation, tests, vet, and\n3159|build:\n3160|\n3161|```bash\n3162|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck\n3163|go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck -section 6.2\n3164|```\n3165|\n3166|The repeated `-section` form is the Story-scope production gate. It resolves\n3167|each assigned subsection, and every heading in a same-top-level range, against\n3168|the immutable v0.7.0 inventory. Every exact `section_binding` must name its own\n3169|production declaration and executable acceptance case, and must additionally\n3170|discharge the whole section it claims. A generic top-level source pin is not a\n3171|scoped implementation owner. Malformed, nonexistent, unpinned, or otherwise\n3172|unowned assignments fail closed.\n3173|\n3174|### Declared coverage and what the gate can decide\n3175|\n3176|A binding that names a real Go declaration and a real acceptance case used to be\n3177|enough. It is not: `section:2.2` named `validateSessionRecordCommon`, which\n3178|validates one enum and a name grammar, while Section 2.2 is the twenty-two\n3179|unconditional lease and replica invariants; `section:18.4` named\n3180|`OpenProjection` while Section 18.4 is audit retention and no retention code\n3181|exists. A Story assigned either section would have found it already owned and\n3182|could have done nothing.\n3183|\n3184|Every `section_binding` now declares a `coverage` level, and the gate recomputes\n3185|that level rather than believing it. The denominator is measured from\n3186|[`internal/specdoc`](internal/specdoc): the RFC 2119 clause lines the pinned\n3187|`SPEC.md` carries under the section's own heading and its subheadings. The\n3188|numerator is the `clauses` the binding enumerates, each of which must name a\n3189|clause of that inventory, quote it verbatim beginning on the exact `SPEC.md`\n3190|line it occupies, and be discharged by an acceptance case the binding itself\n3191|owns.\n3192|\n3193|| Level | Meaning | Admitted as an assigned scope |\n3194|| --- | --- | --- |\n3195|| `full` | every normative clause of the section is enumerated and discharged | yes |\n3196|| `partial` | at least half are | no |\n3197|| `sliver` | fewer than half are | no |\n3198|| `unevidenced` | none are; the registry makes no clause-level claim | no |\n3199|| `unmeasured` | the obligation scanner finds no clause line under the section at all | no |\n3200|\n3201|`unmeasured` is the honest name for what used to be called `declarative` and\n3202|used to be admitted. The scanner matches uppercase RFC 2119 keywords, so a\n3203|section that states its obligations as a table scores zero and was read as\n3204|carrying no obligation. That is false, and the first revision of this gate\n3205|reproduced the very bug it was built to remove: `-section 15.2`, the eighteen-row\n3206|normative exit-code registry, exited 0 with nothing in the tree implementing it,\n3207|and so did `-section 7.3`, the closed Provider Manifest. Nineteen of the 157\n3208|pinned headings are in that class - 7.3, 10.8.1, 13.5, 13.12, 13.14.1-13.14.5,\n3209|14.3, 14.6, 15.2, 16.6, 16.7, 18.2, 19.4 and Appendices A, B and C - and\n3210|`TestUnmeasuredCoverageIsAScannerBlindSpotNotAnAbsenceOfObligation` measures\n3211|that every one of them has a substantive body, so not one is a heading with\n3212|nothing to discharge. Keyword absence is now a failure to measure, never a\n3213|coverage claim.\n3214|\n3215|A binding below `full` must also name its gap, `unmeasured` included, and the\n3216|gap has to name the section as a whole identifier - so a sentence about 6.55 is\n3217|not a gap about 6.5 - and name the production declaration the binding is\n3218|registered to. `unowned_sections` records a section this repository does not\n3219|implement at all, with a gap and the evidence for it; an unowned entry may not\n3220|cover a section the generated catalog requires an owner for, so it is a\n3221|disclosure and never an exemption. Every one of these fields is inside the\n3222|reviewed projection digest, so none of them can be self-minted.\n3223|\n3224|This is what the gate decides, and it is less than semantic coverage. It decides\n3225|that a claimed clause is a real obligation of the claimed section, that it is\n3226|quoted verbatim at the line it occupies, that the discharging acceptance case is\n3227|registered and owned by the binding, and that the declared level equals the\n3228|measured ratio. **It cannot decide that the named acceptance case exercises the\n3229|clause's meaning.** A binding could enumerate every clause of a section and\n3230|point all of them at one weak test, and the gate would admit it. That residual\n3231|class - a complete enumeration discharged by inadequate tests - is not covered\n3232|here and is not claimed to be.\n3233|\n3234|It also cannot see an obligation stated without an RFC 2119 keyword, which is\n3235|why `unmeasured` is refused rather than admitted: the gate reports that it could\n3236|not measure the section instead of inferring that there was nothing to measure.\n3237|And the gap-quality check is a tightening rather than a proof - a sentence that\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
