le its two receiver clauses have no\n3316|implementation; Section 5.5 at 1/3, whose discharged negative-battery clause\n3317|is enforced by identity creation and checking while the opaque-map content\n3318|rule stays half-decided; Section 8 at 4/12, whose discharged probe,\n3319|label-integrity, and row-separation clauses are enforced by the resume tuple\n3320|gate and the native-resume smoke while every materialization rule stays\n3321|unimplemented; and Section 2.2 at 4/22, bound to\n3322|[`internal/fencing`](internal/fencing), whose discharged clauses are the\n3323|single-owner, replica-restraint, winning-epoch-carriage, and\n3324|losing-event-rejection invariants while the replication, secret, store,\n3325|and directory invariants have no implementation; and Section 17.4 at 1/4, bound\n3326|to [`internal/meshneg`](internal/meshneg), whose discharged clause is the\n3327|report-activation-unavailable sentence while upgrade, downgrade, and resume\n3328|flows do not exist), four are `unmeasured` (Sections 7.3, 13.12, 13.14.5 and 15.2, each of\n3329|which carries a gap saying why the scanner measures zero and what is missing),\n3330|and forty-seven are `unevidenced`. Seven sections are recorded unowned.\n3331|All 13 sections added by v0.6.0 name pending task owners in the reviewed\n3332|registry gaps; these assignments grant no runtime admission. The\n3333|[adoption ownership map](internal/traceability/adoption-v0.6.0.md) separates\n3334|shared runtime APIs, their callers, product conformance and upstream source\n3335|publication validators, and preserves historical acceptance obligations.\n3336|The v0.7.0 revision adds no numbered section; its launch-plan, stdin,\n3337|caller_launch_plan, environment_drift and curator-run clause areas name\n3338|pending story owners in the reviewed registry gaps, and these assignments\n3339|grant no runtime admission either. The\n3340|[adoption ownership map](internal/traceability/adoption-v0.7.0.md) attributes\n3341|each clause area to its implementing story and records the shared-section\n3342|splits.\n3343|Assigned-scope admission therefore succeeds today for `-section 6.2`,\n3344|`-section 2.4`, `-section 7.8`, and `-section 10.2` and nothing else; every\n3345|other assignment is refused with its ratio and its gap.\n3346|A `partial` binding is refused by assigned-scope admission exactly like an\n3347|`unevidenced` one: admission requires `full`.\n3348|\n3349|Four admitted bindings out of sixty-eight cover twelve clauses, and that is\n3350|disclosed here rather than hidden: without Section 6.2 the admit path would only\n3351|ever be exercised synthetically. Its discharge is no longer positive-only: the\n3352|native-Windows lanes carry the positive arm and\n3353|`TestDecodeRefusesNonConptyBackendOnNativeWindows` the legacy refusal arm,\n3354|both registered against the `config-versioned-readers` acceptance case.\n3355|Section 2.4 is the first multi-clause admission: its four clauses are\n3356|discharged by the `sessprofile-derive`, `sessprofile-derive-heads`,\n3357|`sessprofile-fork-pair`, and `provhost-mapping-resolution` acceptance cases.\n3358|Sections 7.8 and 10.2 are the clone-story admissions: the seven clauses are\n3359|discharged by the `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`,\n3360|`clone-projection-fidelity`, and `session-adapter-call-binding` acceptance\n3361|cases, each bound to the named suite that executes it.\n3362|\n3363|That is a disclosure of the shipped state, not a target that was met.\n3364|`TestRunRefusesEveryAssignedSectionThatOnlySlivers` and\n3365|`TestVerifyAssignedSectionsRefusesEveryBindingThatOnlySlivers` pin every failing\n3366|binding with its exact measured ratio, so a section that becomes covered has to\n3367|leave those tables deliberately. Five further gaps the disclosure surfaced:\n3368|Section 15.2's code-to-exit registry is implemented in\n3369|[`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror) and checked row by row, and\n3370|[`internal/cliresult`](internal/cliresult) now maps a failure to that exact\n3371|process status through `Emit` and `ExitStatus`, but nothing in the tree calls\n3372|`os.Exit` with it - the only `os.Exit` calls are the `exit(1)` failure paths of\n3373|`cataloggen` and `tracecheck` - so clause `14.2#6` stays undischarged until an\n3374|`ax` binary exists; Section 7.3's closed Provider Manifest exists only as a catalog\n3375|row naming its URN; Section 6.5 requires the `required_capabilities` default to\n3376|be the platform lane minimum while `internal/config/validation.go` accepts only\n3377|an empty default; Section 17.2's single clause is an unknown-event reader\n3378|obligation while its binding now names the CLI Result machine reader `Read`,\n3379|which classifies one completed invocation rather than retaining any event, so it\n3380|does not discharge that clause either - an unknown error code and an inert\n3381|unknown extension are not an unknown session event, and the four numbered reader\n3382|rules that binding does implement carry no RFC 2119 keyword and are invisible to\n3383|the clause scanner; and Section 2.1's single clause is a replica runtime\n3384|obligation that no code here implements.\n3385|\n3386|The Session Adapter host surface lives in\n3387|[`internal/sessadapter`](internal/sessadapter): discovery binding\n3388|(`Discover`), manifest and probe decoding (`DecodeManifest`, `DecodeProbe`),\n3389|the closed fourteen-operation request/success bodies (`CheckRequestBody`,\n3390|`CheckSuccessBody`), resource limits (`DecodeResourceLimits`), the\n3391|request-digest binding and byte-for-byte context echo that carry this\n3392|package's idempotency (`VerifyRequestDigest`, `CheckContextEcho`, and the\n3393|fresh-sink rule), the tuple-registry admission gates\n3394|(`CheckTupleAdmission`), and the per-call execution binding equality\n3395|(`CheckCallBinding`). Eight executable acceptance cases\n3396|(`session-adapter-discovery`, `session-adapter-manifest`,\n3397|`session-adapter-probe`, `session-adapter-operations`,\n3398|`session-adapter-limits`, `session-adapter-idempotency`,\n3399|`session-adapter-tuple-gates`, `session-adapter-call-binding`) bind those\n3400|entry points to their named positive and refusal tests. The Section 7.8\n3401|clause-level binding is `full`: both clauses are enumerated, the\n3402|large-data-by-reference clause against `clone-projection-fidelity` and the\n3403|execution-binding equality clause against `session-adapter-call-binding`.\n3404|Section 13.14.1 carries no RFC 2119 clause line the scanner can see, so no\n3405|registry binding enumerates it; its clause record is the three package\n3406|`TRACEABILITY.md` files and the three leaf conformance matrices, executed\n3407|by the `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`, and\n3408|`clone-projection-fidelity` suites.\n3409|\n3410|The Directory Node host surface lives in\n3411|[`internal/dirnode`](internal/dirnode): the two-major manifest\n3412|bootstrap (`DecideBootstrapStep` with its exact downgrade tuple,\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
