{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000df6f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0b3cf-5753-7b41-a2b3-ce03595a21fa"},"sequence":3602,"recorded_at":1780531400007199,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"f856bb23-ad72-4bdf-8e88-2c200bbb093c"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0b3eb-95f1-7aa3-bb5e-5bbd30f30500"},"task_id":"01a0b3eb-95f1-7aa3-bb5e-5bbd30f30500","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0b3eb-95f1-7aa3-bb5e-5bbd30f30500","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-76-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cd /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1cyj0q/worktree\\nhead -n 40 LOGBOOK.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read LOGBOOK head\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-18\\n\\n### TASK-260830-32ypr2 — projection fidelity over captured bytes (FINAL leaf, STORY-260830-1cyj0q)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/cloneproject` implements the Section 13.14.1 projection-fidelity closure — `Normalize` derives a Canonical Session + Canonical Events from a sealed Clone Capture Manifest, its sealed Clone Raw Object Manifest, and blob bytes fetched through the real store layout. Unknown native types and unknown-class members become raw-addressable `opaque_event` records (`unknown_native_event`, ranges resolve to exact bytes); foreign encrypted/signed reasoning becomes byte-exact `opaque_reasoning` (`foreign_encrypted_payload`/`foreign_signature_unverifiable`, no content members); foreign instructions pin `low` authority and never reach the effective snapshot; tool calls resolve `completed` only with their result, else `aborted` history (`unsafe_pending_action`) with an always-empty live surface (pending needs a live work order, which capture never carries); source usage counts source-only; text over 64 KiB becomes an installed overflow blob reference (65536 inline / 65537 referenced, byte-exact). Every proof runs the real `clonesnap.Capture` entry first; every sealed byte re-decodes before return.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (25 tests incl. the 33-row refusal table plus unstable/drift entries, determinism, idempotent replay, no-partial-bundle failure; 88.9% statement coverage); 49 narrowing mutants KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED, battery run twice with per-plant raw logs (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including two token-preserving rows killed by the behavioral suite and one verified cross-kill (the encrypted-gate plant also reddens the protected-message test). No `ax` command/doctor/capability claim; clause map + per-kind fact registry in `internal/cloneproject/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- STORY-CLOSE: registry `section:7.8` and `section:10.2` unevidenced→full (2/2 + 5/5, excerpts re-measured, pin re-derived `69d156d9…2235052a` via the gate, shown in results); new acceptance cases `clone-capture-contracts`, `clone-native-capture`, `clone-projection-fidelity`, `session-adapter-call-binding`; `tracecheck` green at cases=144, full=4, partial=8, sliver=5, unevidenced=47, clauses 63/569 with `--section 7.8` and `--section 10.2` admitted; `section:13.14.1` deliberately unbound (scanner sees no RFC 2119 line — closed-shape sentences only — so a binding would measure `unmeasured` and fail assigned scope; record lives in the three TRACEABILITY files + matrices). Pin tests updated (report wants, sliver tables, 10.2 rename row now attacks `Capture`, admits lists extended to 7.8/10.2, README figure pins with `twelve`/`forty-seven`); README package section + measured-coverage rewrite (fenced line byte-equal).\\n- REFRESH: this run opened on stale base `a12d1bd` (branch tip `47294bb`) while trunk was `c3aae73`, so `refresh-candidate` ran FIRST (`refresh_advanced` onto `c3aae73`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay keeping trunk's 4qojoz entry newest-first). The audit restored trunk bytes for every carried stale revert (`.task-board`, `internal/meshneg`, `internal/rpcwire` tests/harness, `internal/matjournal` test, `task-board.config.json` back to the 30-command form); README/LOGBOOK/traceability edits were re-applied purely additively on the new bytes and the ownership registry MERGED (trunk's 5 cases + 3 upgraded bindings kept, this story's 4 cases + 2 bindings appended/transplanted — never replaced). Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 7 bounded groups incl. sessquery alone, 41/41 packages, no DATA RACE).\\n- BOUNDS (sibling scope, not waived): fixture-native record envelope is test-defined framing (body shapes exact, envelope extras unclaimed); fact registries only for emitted kinds; native-protected records carry no reason code; turn IDs/source times null; call arguments not carried; SYNTHESIZED/partial/unavailable statuses and non-text content blocks never emitted (shape rules owned by the accepted clonebundle suite); 13.14.2–13.14.5 (fidelity dispositions, planning, lineage, transaction, tuple admission) sibling-owned; 7.8 operation frames stay `sessadapter`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n- AC: 24 of 24 rows driven through `Normalize` by named tests and measured with narrowings (matrix in `TASK-260830-32ypr2_conformance-matrix.md`).\\n\\n### STORY-260830-4qojoz (mesh-rpc-framing-and-negotiation) — final leaf TASK-260830-19bjfj rev2: adversarial closure on the adopted v0.7.0 registry\\n- REWORK (test-only; no production behavior file changed): rev1 was reviewed CHANGES REQUESTED on the story-close half only — its technical body (N1-N3 closure, mutants, fuzz controls, 23/29 AC ratio) was independently reproduced by the reviewer. Rev1 was built on stale base 888ae3d while trunk adopted v0.7.0 (2fc6d50) mid-run. Rev2 refreshed the candidate onto 2fc6d50 (`refresh_advanced`, checkpoint-bound LOGBOOK replay: trunk's two v0.7.0 entries kept newest-first, 219okr block carried verbatim below them) and re-based every story-close edit on trunk bytes.\\n- TRACEABILITY: registry work moved into adopted `ownership.v0.7.0.json` (5 new acceptance cases, 3 upgraded bindings: 11.2 partial 3/5, 17.1 partial 3/6, 17.4 sliver 1/4); every clause line re-measured against the pinned v0.7.0 document through the production clause inventory (11.2: 7364/7408/7420; 17.1: 15567/15589/15602; 17.4: 15661). The invented 11.3#18 binding is dropped — no production code parses a digest-identity array, so 11.3 stays the carried unevidenced stub and `rpcwire-inventory-arrays` was not ported. Digest re-derived `b4ae9091…` (gate-computed, shown in results). tracecheck green `56/569` (+7); section runs refuse admission with the measured ratios, quoted verbatim. Deliberate pins: `traceability_test.go`/`main_test.go` figure tables, the README pin test's closed number-word map extended with `eight`/`forty-nine`, and a reviewed-upgrade extension to `TestV070RegistryRederivesFromTrunkV060Registry` (each upgraded binding/case pinned literally, new clauses re-measured; every other binding still rederives byte-equal).\\n- P3 GAPS (all closed with a failing-without-it test): opaque-body object gate over `health.get` (`[]`/`null`/`\\\"x\\\"`/`42`/duplicate-member → ErrFrame) + `FuzzClosedOperationBodies` now feeds raw bodies with an I-JSON object oracle (the naive `&& op !=` plant is vacuous — the stale `err` still propagates — so the committed probe restructures the gate); changed-body retry after a committed effect → literal `idempotency_mismatch` with a single retained journal (one-off J1 overlay kills the new test, staging still passes); body-fuzzer oracle bound stated explicitly (member-name + object + round-trip only; bounds/vocabularies owned by the unit suite) + hello-body-extra seed in `FuzzUnknownFields`; exact 8388608-admit/8388609-refuse encode edge; `ErrVersionMismatch` class pinned in the error-schema lanes; literal `[2 3 4]`/`[5]` offer sets in the N2 rows; nonce-alphabet plant widened to the full unpadded standard-base64 class (two-arm `RawStdEncoding` narrowing, no new import).\\n- MUTANTS: meshneg 37 killed / neutral passed / detail-text SURVIVED (exit 0); rpcwire 41 killed / neutral passed / error-text SURVIVED (exit 0). Fuzz controls re-run on the new targets: all three FAIL on their plants (exit 1) plus the two new P3 control proofs. Full 30-command suite green on the refreshed tree (race gate in 5 chunks, sessquery alone; no DATA RACE). Per-plant raw logs + tables in the outcome tar; `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`.\\n- BOUNDS (stated, not green): 22/24 op bodies opaque; no minor-selection entry; envelope request_id correlation-only (replay/idempotency adopted from matjournal plus the new committed-phase pin); chunk-data base64 unwitnessed (strictness pinned at the nonce gate); RPC layer mutates nothing (purity bound). AC: 23 of 29 rows driven through production entries by named tests, 6 declared stated bounds (matrix in the outcome evidence).\\n- Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for handoff snapshot; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2g5be6 — native capture and source-race check (second leaf)\\n\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/clonesnap` implements the Section 13.14.1 capture operation over a real fixture store — contained walk (`secprim` Guard opens, symlink-intermediate/FIFO/dir refusals naming the member), nine-class classification with always-excluded bytes never opened, Capture Boundary from measured evidence (stable proof or core-created `unstable_archive`), a source-race gate comparing content digests before any seal, workspace checkpoint + source head from observed state, Section 10.2 descriptors (empty/multi-chunk) with `capability_unavailable` past 128 GiB, and target admission (`RefuseUnstableForTarget`, `RefuseMaximalSafeUnlessComplete`) emitting an admission receipt. Every manifest seals through the landed `clonebundle` builders and re-decodes before publish; every byte installs through `localstore` no-replace.\\n- ORDERING (the task's named check): the sealed stable proof carries the two measured source digests (pre and post) — the gate proved them equal before the seal ran, so the sealed bytes equal either measurement — and the ordering mutants prove the gate precedes the seal at both entries: `N-race-order-capture` (manifest scan), `N-race-order-project` (seal error message), `N-race-order-project-seal` (capture-store scan at the projection entry). Changed byte/size, appended record, replaced/removed file, excluded size change, and unreadable-at-post each refuse or seal `unstable_archive` with `source_not_quiescent`, never silently stable.\\n- EVIDENCE: package suite green (positives, full refusal table, 4-class leak scan over blobs/manifests/logs/errors, digest-only log assertions, every-payload-blob-installed assertion after Capture and after the crash replay, target-sink-empty assertion on the archive path, real-SIGKILL crash test with replay convergence + clean-run byte equality, idempotent triple-project); 41 narrowing + 2 add-write rows KILLED + harmless control SURVIVED (`testdata/mutant_harness.py --log-dir`, one raw log per plant with subprocess exit, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, no `__pycache__`), including the token-preserving prefix mutant killed by the behavioral Capture entry and the cross-package P3-ε row (plant in clonebundle, killer here). No `internal/traceability` edit (FINAL leaf carries bindings + re-pin); clause map in `internal/clonesnap/TRACEABILITY.md`.\\n- REV3 (rework of review RUN-260918-fdce92; no base move, still `2f844bb` over trunk `a12d1bd`; `origin/main` still `c3aae73`): row 8 sealed unstable pre/post digests + generation asserted against the measurements (`N-u