nism (30), agreement arms (31), protected-tool fold-skip\n+  (32), result-status vocabulary (33), size arm (34), trailing\n+  bytes (35), unknown+protected body decision (36).\n+- Pinned bounds (37–38): non-JSONL included members refuse;\n+  null directives decode as empty.\n+\n+Measured, not planned: every gate row carries a directly-reddening\n+narrowing (62 narrowings + 2 labelled rows, battery green twice).\n+Disclosed non-narrowed members: row 15 post-boundary (gate-level\n+only — the same `resolveToolCalls` decision row 13 narrows);\n+rows 18/19/21 shape internals (owned by the accepted clonebundle\n+suite, stated per member); row 24 (failure-injection proofs, no\n+gate); row 37 (enforcing gate narrowed by the strict-decode rows);\n+row 38 (admitted shape, no gate). No row is prose-only.\n+\n+## Mutants\n+\n+`internal/cloneproject/testdata/mutant_harness.py`: 62 narrowing\n+rows + 2 labelled non-narrowing rows (`N-empty-projection`\n+single-member class, `N-overflow-truncate` behaviour swap) +\n+harmless `C-doc-comment` SURVIVED control. Battery executed TWICE\n+on the final tree, exit 0 both runs, 65/65 `ok:` lines each, one\n+raw log per plant per run carrying the mutant identity, patch,\n+subprocess exit, and FAIL line (`mutants/run1/`, `mutants/run2/`,\n+`run1-battery.log`, `run2-battery.log` in the archive).\n+Token-preserving rows: `N-native-type-token` and\n+`N-protection-encrypted` — both killers execute the behavioral\n+`Normalize` suite over captured bytes. No plant covers two sites.\n+`PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, zero `__pycache__`/`.pyc` (verified\n+after the runs). Cross-check: the six re-anchorable rev1 reviewer\n+plant shapes (R1 actors-unsorted, R2 encrypted-admits-signed,\n+R5 protected-tools-folded, R6 status-pending, R7 size-skipped,\n+R8 unknown-protected-skipped) were applied by hand to the final\n+tree and all KILLED firsthand by the new tests; R3/R3b are the\n+stated P3-c bound and R4's anchor is deleted by the delegation\n+(covered by `